\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 0. Mission, Modes, Identity & Cognitive Agents\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section defines why the OS Dashboard AI Assistant exists, which actors (human and machine) operate within it, and how those actors behave across deployment modes. Its contents are normative for the rest of the specification: later sections (drivers, Capsules, planes, Meta-Stack) must remain consistent with these mission, identity, and cognitive contracts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 0.1 Mission, Product Scope & Strategic Objectives\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 0.1.1 Mission The OS Dashboard AI Assistant (\'93OS Dashboard\'94, \'93the OS\'94) is a driver-aware AI operating system for knowledge and execution work. Its mission is to:\
Govern, automate, and augment the full lifecycle of high-value work across:\
Documents, code, research, simulations, writing, finance, security, and operations.\
\'95 Turn real workflows into executable Capsules (repeatable workflows + environments) that can be run, audited, shared,\
and improved over time.\
\'95 Provide a single, auditable control surface over:\
OS and Unix execution, package & environment topologies,\
\uc0\u9675  SaaS and infra APIs, databases and research tools,\
\uc0\u9675  Policies, billing, compliance, and regulator views.\
\'95 Enable governed autonomy: AI agents can act on files, tools, systems, and infra\'97but only through governed drivers\
and Capsules, under explicit policy and with full traceability.\
\'95 The system must serve simultaneously as:\
A local polymath workstation (desktop + CLI) that behaves like a personal \'93Jarvis\'94 on a single machine.\
\'95 An enterprise AI OS (multi-tenant backend + governance + marketplace) that can be adopted by teams, companies,\
and regulators, with regulator-grade audit and policy enforcement.\
\'95 A foundation for cross-org / civilization-scale coordination through higher Meta-Stack layers (Advanced \uc0\u8594  Super \u8594 \
Hyper \uc0\u8594  Ultra \u8594  God).\
\'95 0.1.2 Product Scope\
In scope Driver-aware orchestrator Intent capture, planning, and execution over:\
OS/Unix, package managers, SaaS APIs, DBs, clusters, lab devices.\
\uc0\u9675  Strictly mediated through drivers and Capsules, not ad-hoc shell access.\
1. Plane-based platform Data Plane \'96 CIR, Ledger, Capsule artifacts, indices, observability stores.\
\uc0\u9675  Control Plane \'96 Orchestrator, workflows, driver calls, daemons.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance Plane \'96 Identity, policy, compliance, billing, regulator fabric.\
2. Workspaces / Domain Engines Master Stack & Project Management Engine.\
\uc0\u9675  Dev & DevOps workspace (Merge Advisor, Commit\u8594 Task, CI/CD).\
\uc0\u9675  Research & Simulation workspace (Unified Lab, Simulation Hub, Digital Twins).\
\uc0\u9675  Writer workspace (Writer Workstation Engine, canon & lore).\
\uc0\u9675  Archive / Continuity / Resonance workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  Cybersecurity workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  Business / Finance workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  Record Auditor & Logbook workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  Operator / SRE workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  Digital Twin & Enterprise Twin workspace.\
3. Capsule System & Marketplace E t bl C l C l P k D i P k P f i OS b dl\
\'a0\
\'a0\
4. Executable Capsules, Capsule Packs, Driver Packs, Profession OS bundles.\
\uc0\u9675  Workflow \u8594  App Synthesizer, Environment Blueprints, Operator Studio.\
\uc0\u9675  My Stack Capsules and cross-Capsule composition.\
\uc0\u9675  Meta-Stack Capability Layers\
Structured capability ladder from Core capabilities to Advanced/Super/Hyper/Ultra/God layers (detailed in Section 17).\
\uc0\u9675  Meta-systems (ARC, Cognitive Twin Fabric, Canon of Truth, Reality Contract Layer, etc.) built on the same core\
substrate. 5. Out of scope (for this spec / v1) Implementing a new general-purpose OS kernel or window manager; OS Dashboard runs on top of existing OSes.\
\'95 Replacing all existing MDM/endpoint tooling; it integrates with and orchestrates them where needed.\
\'95 Providing consumer social features (feeds, messaging unrelated to work) or generic \'93super-app\'94 behavior.\
\'95 Physical robotics and actuation beyond what is reachable via existing, governed APIs and drivers in v1.\
\'95 Acting as a monolithic data warehouse; instead, it indexes and orchestrates across existing stores.\
\'95 0.1.3 Strategic Objectives\
Governed AI OS for knowledge work Become the canonical governed AI OS that sits across documents, code, infra, and workflows with regulator-grade audit and policy surfaces. 1. Executable workflow & Capsule platform Provide the default substrate for executable Capsules (repeatable workflows + environments) and their marketplace, spanning individual, team, and cross-org use. 2. Continuity-aware cognitive partner Act as a long-memory, continuity-aware assistant that understands projects, theories, and organizations over years, grounded in CIR, Ledger, Archive, twins, and TRF. 3. Driver-first execution fabric Normalize all external capabilities\'97OS, Unix commands, package managers, SaaS APIs, DBs, HPC clusters, lab devices\'97as governed drivers with manifests, policies, costs, and observability. 4. Extensible, modular, self-improving platform Allow new drivers, Capsules, plugins, workspaces, and policies to be added without core rewrites, and continuously improve via mining execution traces, Ledger history, Capsule performance, and Project Intelligence. 5. Regulator-acceptable automation of high-stakes work Make AI-driven automation acceptable in regulated and safety-critical settings by default via policy enforcement, auditability, Evidence Packs, and Regulator Fabric views. 6. Model-provider agnostic yet optimized Treat GPT-5.1 Pro / GPT-5.1 Thinking and similar models as current engines but design the Model Layer to be pluggable, cost-aware, and policy-aware. 7. Path from individual OS to civilization fabric Provide a clear path from individual productivity (Local Mode) to enterprise coordination to inter-OS federation and civilization-scale Meta-Stack capabilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 0.2 Design Principles, Constraints, Assumptions & Non-Goals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 0.2.1 Core Design Principles Auditable by construction Every meaningful action (model call, driver call, Capsule run, environment change, policy decision) is recorded in the Project Ledger and observable via Record Auditor and Evidence Packs. The system must always be able to answer:\
\'93Who/what did what, when, under which policy, with which environment and inputs?\'94 1. Driver-first, not tool-first All external capabilities (OS, Unix, package managers, SaaS APIs, DBs, lab tools) are exposed as drivers with manifests, not opaque tools or ad-hoc shell access. Unix/Kernel execution and package managers are treated as first-class, governed drivers, not side channels. 2. Plane separation (Data / Control / Governance) Data motion (CIR, Ledger, indices), control decisions (plans, driver orchestration), and governance decisions (policies, budgets, compliance) are logically separated, even when co-located physically. This enables reasoning, scaling, and safety. 3. Local \uc0\u8801  Enterprise (conceptually) Local and Enterprise modes share the same conceptual architecture and domain model. Differences lie in scale, driver scope, trust boundaries, and governance strictness\'97not in vocabulary or semantics. 4. Domain-neutral substrate, domain-rich surfaces Core abstractions (Projects, Tasks, CIR, Capsules, Drivers, Policies, Twins) are domain-agnostic. Workspaces and Engines compose these into domain-specific UX and behavior (Dev, Research, Writer, Cyber, Finance, etc.). 5. Governable automation Automation is always subject to policy evaluation budget checks and safety harnesses especially for System\
\'a0\
\'a0\
6. Automation is always subject to policy evaluation, budget checks, and safety harnesses\'97especially for System Execution and Package & Environment drivers. There is no unguarded \'93root shell\'94 for agents. Self-improving over time The platform continuously learns from execution traces, Capsule performance, Ledger history, and TRF/AIC insights to refine:\
Plans and strategies,\
\uc0\u9675  Environment specs and blueprints,\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule templates and packs,\
\uc0\u9675  Policies and guardrails.\
7. Layered Meta-Stack with graceful degradation Advanced/Super/Hyper/Ultra/God layer capabilities are explicit and optional. Each higher layer must degrade cleanly if disabled, without corrupting the core. 8. Local-first optionality & offline resilience Local Mode must be able to function with degraded or zero network connectivity and, where possible, with local or cached models, deferring sync of ledger and evidence. 9. Explainable cognitive behavior Personas and daemons must produce reasoning traces, references, and justifications suitable for human review, audit, and scientific scrutiny. 10. Reusability & modularity Repeated patterns in workflows, policies, simulations, or analyses should be expressible as Capsules, Blueprints, Template Packs, or Policies that are versioned and sharable. 11. 0.2.2 Constraints & Assumptions Runs on top of existing OSes OS Dashboard is not a bare-metal kernel; it runs atop Windows, macOS, and Linux.\
\'95 Unreliable external systems\
All external systems (APIs, CLIs, OS environments, SaaS) are assumed unreliable; the design must include retries, backoffs, fallbacks, idempotency, and degraded modes.\
\'95 Heterogeneous estate\
Must support mixed environments:\
Windows/macOS/Linux, on-prem and cloud,\
\uc0\u9675  Modern SaaS, legacy UIs, air-gapped lab machines.\
\'95 Multi-model, evolving Model Layer\
Multiple model providers and on-prem models will coexist, with evolving capabilities; the Model Layer is pluggable and cost-aware.\
\'95 Regulated contexts\
Enterprise Mode assumes regulator presence or future regulator interest; explainability, reproducibility, and data residency are non-negotiable requirements in many deployments.\
\'95 Sandboxed execution\
For risky workflows (system commands, package installs, simulations), containerization/virtualization and Safety Harnesses must be available.\
\'95 0.2.3 Non-Goals (for this spec / v1)\
Replacing every existing MDM/endpoint or SIEM system; instead, integrate with and augment them.\
\'95 Prescribing a single vendor for models, storage, or orchestration; these remain pluggable.\
\'95 Providing full UX design or visual styling specifications beyond what is needed to express architectural requirements\
(personas, approvals, evidence views, etc.).\
\'95 Implementing a generic programming language or low-level VM beyond what Capsule and Policy representations\
require.\
\'95 Serving as a general-purpose, consumer-grade chat assistant unrelated to projects, drivers, or Capsules.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 0.3 Deployment Modes Overview (Local, Cloud, Enterprise, Hybrid, Offline-First)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The conceptual stack (domain model, planes, Capsules, drivers) is identical across modes; what changes is scale, infra components, trust boundaries, and enabled drivers. 0.3.1 Local Mode (Solo / Power User) Purpose \'93Jarvis for one polymath\'94 on a single machine: a local OS for projects, research, writing, finances, and experiments, with high control and minimal external dependencies.\
\'95 Characteristics\
Desktop GUI and CLI on a local runtime.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Desktop GUI and CLI on a local runtime.\
Local metadata and state:\
SQLite or embedded DBs for domain entities.\
\uc0\u9675  Local filesystem plus optional local vector/search indices.\
\'95 Direct access to:\
Filesystem, processes, windowing, local Git repos.\
\uc0\u9675  Local System Execution (shell/terminal) and Package & Env drivers.\
\uc0\u9675  Local research tools and simulations.\
\'95 Connectors (optional, user-controlled)\
Cloud storage (OneDrive, Google Drive, S3-like).\
\'95 Git hosting (GitHub, GitLab).\
\'95 Productivity suites (Office, Google Workspace).\
\'95 Email/calendar and ticketing.\
\'95 Governance posture\
Governance plane is advisory by default; user is effectively sovereign.\
\'95 Users can opt into stricter local policies (e.g., Safety Harness for particular commands, local data vaults).\
\'95 Failure & Recovery\
Loss of network must not compromise:\
Access to CIR, Ledger, Capsules, Blueprints.\
\uc0\u9675  Execution of local Capsules and drivers.\
\'95 Sync conflicts (if syncing to a cloud tenant) resolved via:\
Ledger-based reconciliation and user-visible conflict views.\
\'95 0.3.2 Cloud / Enterprise Mode (Org / Multi-Tenant)\
Purpose Multi-tenant backend for organizations, with strong isolation, governance, billing, and regulator-grade observability.\
\'95 Characteristics\
Cluster-based backend (API/ASGI services) providing:\
Multi-tenant relational DB for Users, Tenants, Projects, Tasks, Policies, Usage.\
\uc0\u9675  Object store for CIR, artifacts, Capsules, Evidence Packs.\
\uc0\u9675  Search & vector indices for retrieval and research graphs.\
\uc0\u9675  Queues and workers for daemons, driver orchestration, Capsule execution.\
\'95 Integrations:\
Identity: SSO (OIDC/SAML), directory, HRIS, SCIM provisioning.\
\uc0\u9675  Productivity & DevOps: Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, GitHub/GitLab, ticketing, CI/CD.\
\uc0\u9675  Finance & Ops: ERP, accounting, billing systems.\
\'95 Driver scope\
Central driver registry with:\
Org-wide drivers (SaaS, DBs, clusters).\
\uc0\u9675  Tenant-scoped drivers and environment profiles.\
\'95 System Execution & Package drivers typically run on dedicated worker hosts/bastions, under strict policy.\
\'95 Governance posture\
Strong RBAC/ABAC controls over all entities.\
\'95 Policy engine enforced on:\
Model calls (data classification),\
\uc0\u9675  Driver invocations (scope, arguments),\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule deployments and promotions.\
\'95 Failure & Recovery\
Tenant isolation: failures in one tenant must not affect others.\
\'95 Graceful degradation:\
Read-only modes for CIR and Ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Prioritized shedding of non-critical daemons before core flows.\
\'95 0.3.3 Hybrid, Edge & Offline-First\
\'a0\
\'a0\
Hybrid Mode Local Desktop + Enterprise Cluster:\
Local instance handles close-to-user drivers (filesystem, IDE, compilers, local simulations).\
\uc0\u9675  Enterprise cluster handles central Ledger of record, cross-team Capsules, heavy model calls, and governance.\
\'95 Hybrid Capsules:\
Some steps run locally; others run in cluster.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy controls where certain steps are allowed (e.g., sensitive data only on-prem).\
\'95 Edge / Air-Gapped / Lab Nodes\
Local OS Dashboard instances with restricted driver sets (no Internet; internal lab tools only).\
\'95 Emphasis on:\
System Execution, Package & Env drivers.\
\uc0\u9675  Local research tools, lab devices, simulations.\
\'95 Asynchronous evidence syncing:\
When connectivity exists, Evidence Packs and summarized ledger events can be exported/imported.\
\'95 Offline-First Guarantees\
Define minimum offline capabilities:\
Project views, Master Stack, local Capsules, local drivers.\
