\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 0.9 Terminology, Glossary & Canonical Definitions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This spec uses the following canonical definitions (extended glossary lives in an appendix; AIC is responsible for maintaining canon):\
Project \'96 Coherent initiative grouping tasks, artifacts, environments, Capsules, and policies (e.g., \'93Trading Engine v2\'94, \'93Book Series\'94, \'93Lab Program\'94).\
\'95 Workspace / Domain Engine \'96 Domain-specific view and toolset over Projects (Dev, Research, Writer, Cyber, Finance,\
Archive, Operator, Twin).\
\'95 Task \'96 Atomic unit of work tied to a project and often bound to a persona or agent.\
\'95 Master Stack \'96 Cross-project prioritized view of all tasks and initiatives, governed by Sora and informed by\
Finance/Strategy and Archive.\
\'95 CIR (Canonical Internal Representation) \'96 Format-agnostic representation of content (documents, code, tables, plots,\
configs) used for reasoning, diffing, and synchronization.\
\'95 Ledger / Project Ledger \'96 Append-only, tamper-evident event log capturing material actions and decisions (commits,\
Capsule runs, environment changes, policy evaluations, approvals).\
\'95 Driver \'96 Governed connector to an OS, software, data source, or infra capability, described by a manifest (capabilities,\
constraints, costs, observability, policies).\
\'95 Capsule \'96 Versioned, executable workflow unit with:\
A driver graph and environment spec,\
\uc0\u9675  Inputs/outputs and tests,\
\uc0\u9675  Metadata (owner, domain, risk classification),\
\uc0\u9675  Links to CIR and Ledger events.\
\'95 Capsule Pack \'96 Curated set of related Capsules, blueprints, and templates for a domain (e.g., \'93Creator OS Pack\'94,\
\'93Quant OS Pack\'94, \'93SRE Incident Pack\'94).\
\'95 Environment Blueprint \'96 Declarative spec describing required packages, tools, and configurations for a\
machine/role/project (e.g., \'93Backend Dev Env v3\'94).\
\'95 Twin (Digital / Cognitive / Enterprise / Reality) \'96 Structured models of systems, devices, organizations, or personas\
used for simulation, analysis, and planning.\
\'95 Persona \'96 Strategy bundle over the same substrate, defined by goals, scopes, and behavior patterns (e.g., Chris,\
Sora, Aria, AIC).\
\'95 Daemon \'96 Non-interactive cognitive agent executing within defined scopes and budgets, producing monitoring,\
analysis, or optimization outputs.\
\'95 Evidence Pack \'96 Bundled set of logs, Ledger events, artifacts, environment captures, and justifications sufficient to\
support a claim, release, or audit.\
\'95 Planes (Data / Control / Governance) \'96 Conceptual divisions separating information, orchestration, and\
policy/economics.\
\'95 These terms are authoritative and must be used consistently across all sections.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

