\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 1.2.1 Ingress / Edge Architecture (Industry-Standard Front Door) Purpose Define the canonical ingress pattern for all deployment modes (Local, Cloud, Enterprise, Hybrid) such that:\
Every request is authenticated, authorized, rate-limited, policy-checked, and auditable.\
\uc0\u9675  Implementation Requirements\
The system SHOULD implement the following edge stack (physically separate in Enterprise mode; logically present in Local mode):\
Load Balancer / Reverse Proxy:\
TLS termination, L7 routing, connection pooling.\
\uc0\u9675  API Gateway:\
Request validation, schema enforcement, auth integration, routing to Control Plane APIs.\
\uc0\u9675  WAF / Abuse Controls (Enterprise recommended):\
DDoS mitigation, bot filtering, request anomaly detection.\
\uc0\u9675  Rate Limiting + Admission Control:\
Per-user, per-tenant, per-workspace, and per-capability throttles.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy Enforcement Point (PEP) at the edge:\
Every request MUST pass through a PEP that consults the Policy Decision Point (PDP) prior to any privileged action.\
\uc0\u9675  Notes by Mode\
Local Mode:\
The \'93edge\'94 MAY be an embedded gateway (localhost) but MUST preserve the same logical enforcement points and audit logs.\
\uc0\u9675  Enterprise Mode:\
Gateway MUST be horizontally scalable and support tenant isolation (RBAC/ABAC) and per-tenant quotas.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  1.2.2 Model Router / Inference Gateway (Provider Abstraction + Reliability)\
Purpose Provide a capability-aware routing layer for all model calls (LLM, multimodal, local models, third-party providers) so that:\
The Orchestrator is decoupled from any single model vendor.\
\uc0\u9675  Cost, latency, and reliability are controlled and metered.\
\uc0\u9675  Data residency and confidentiality constraints are enforced.\
\uc0\u9675  Core Responsibilities\
Capability routing:\
Select model/provider based on modality, required tools, reasoning tier, latency budget, and risk tier.\
\uc0\u9675  Fallback + escalation:\
On failure or low-confidence outcomes, retry or escalate to a higher-tier model per policy.\
\uc0\u9675  Budget enforcement:\
Reject or downshift requests that exceed configured budgets; log all decisions.\
\uc0\u9675  Privacy + residency enforcement:\
Prevent restricted data from leaving approved boundaries; support redaction/tokenization where required.\
\uc0\u9675  Observability:\
Emit ModelCall records (with approved redaction) into Ledger/Audit/Usage Fabric.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  1.2.3 Control Plane Service Decomposition (Minimum Set)\
The following logical components are recommended as first-class services (or modules in Local mode):\
assistant_core Orchestrator:\
Intent\uc0\u8594 Context\u8594 Plan orchestration, tool/driver coordination, outcome synthesis.\
\uc0\u9675  Workflow Engine:\
Plan graph execution, retries/compensation, scheduling, dependency management.\
\uc0\u9675  Driver Fabric:\
Driver registry, capability discovery, invocation routing, contract enforcement, per-driver throttles.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule Runtime:\
Manifest resolution, environment provisioning, sandbox execution, artifact capture, recording/replay.\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence & Provenance Collector:\
Standardizes run records, evidence packs, policy decisions, and links them to Ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Notification & Activity Stream:\
User-facing \'93what happened\'94 stream (replaces generic \'93feed\'94 semantics).\
\uc0\u9675  Search/Indexing Workers:\
Async indexing of CIR/Ledger/Capsule metadata for retrieval.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  1.2.4 Asynchronous Execution Backbone (Queues, Topics, Workers)\
Principle All long-running, high-latency, or failure-prone operations MUST be executed asynchronously via the execution backbone:\
Driver invocations.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule builds/runs.\
\uc0\u9675  Indexing/backfills.\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence pack generation.\
\uc0\u9675  Recommended Topics / Queues (logical names)\
driver.invocations capsule.runs ledger.events policy.decisions usage.records index.updates notifications.user deadletter.* Implementation Notes Idempotency keys MUST be supported for driver/capsule operations (at-least-once delivery tolerant).\
\uc0\u9675  Dead-letter queues MUST exist with operator tooling for re-drive and investigation.\
\uc0\u9675  Priority lanes SHOULD exist for interactive user flows vs batch/backfill workloads.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 1.2.5 Evidence, Audit, and Replay as First-Class Outputs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Invariant No privileged action is considered \'93complete\'94 unless it produces:\
A Ledger event linking intent\uc0\u8594 plan\u8594 driver/capsule execution.\
\uc0\u9675  An audit log entry suitable for regulator-grade review (subject to redaction rules).\
\uc0\u9675  A reproducibility envelope: environment snapshot references, artifacts, and policy decisions.\
\uc0\u9675  At runtime, OS Dashboard follows a consistent Intent \u8594  Context \u8594  Plan \u8594  Policy \u8594  Execution \u8594  Evidence \u8594  Learning\
pattern. 1. Intent Capture (Presentation \uc0\u8594  Application) Sources:\
User chat, UI buttons, CLI commands, scheduler/cron, webhooks, daemons.\
\'95 Each is normalized into an Intent object:\
Actor, tenant, project, workspace, goal, constraints, initial risk tier.\
\'95 2. Context Assembly (Application + Domain + Drivers)\
Application uses Domain APIs, search, and driver manifests to build a Context Bundle:\
Relevant Projects/Tasks, CIR slices, Capsule graph, environment specs,\
\uc0\u9675  Driver capabilities and costs,\
\uc0\u9675  Policy snapshot (applicable policies, budgets, safety harness rules).\
\'95 3. Driver-Aware Planning (Application \uc0\u8594  Cognitive)\
Cognitive Layer (persona + daemons + TRF) consumes the Context Bundle and returns one or more Driver Execution Plans:\
Graphs of Capsule invocations and driver operations,\
\uc0\u9675  Preconditions, postconditions, success criteria,\
\uc0\u9675  Estimated cost/latency, risk levels, required approvals.\
\'95 4. Governance Pre-Check (Application \uc0\u8594  Governance)\
Plans are evaluated by Policy Engine and Billing Fabric:\
Deny / transform / annotate / approve with conditions.\
\'95 May require explicit human approval (per role or multi-party).\
\'95 5. Human-in-the-Loop Review (Presentation)\
For plans above configured thresholds:\
UI shows plan summary, resources, risk notes, cost envelope, environment changes.\
\'95 Users can:\
Approve, edit parameters, or cancel.\
\'95 6. Execution (Application \uc0\u8594  Driver Fabric \u8594  Infrastructure)\
Driver Execution Fabric dispatches steps across:\
OS Drivers, Unix/System Execution Layer, Package & Env Drivers,\
\uc0\u9675  Software/SaaS, Data, Workflow, Research/HPC drivers.\
\'95 Capsules orchestrate multi-step flows:\
With sandboxing and resource constraints.\
\'95 7. Recording & Evidence (Application \uc0\u8594  Domain & Governance)\
Every material step:\
Appended as ProjectEvents in Ledger,\
\uc0\u9675  Logged in audit logs + usage records,\
\uc0\u9675  Potentially assembled into Evidence Packs for releases/incidents/audits.\
\'95 8. Feedback & Learning (Application \uc0\u8594  Cognitive)\
Outcomes feed back into:\
Personas and daemons (for learning),\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 (\
g), Capsule templates and blueprints (Self-Evolving Capsule Ecosystem),\
\uc0\u9675  Policy tuning and budgets (Billing Optimizer).\
\uc0\u9675  This pattern is invariant across Local vs Enterprise and across all workspaces.\
1.3 Architectural Principles These principles constrain all design and implementation decisions. Auditable by Construction Every significant action (model call, driver invocation, environment change, policy decision) produces ledger and audit events.\
\uc0\u9675  No \'93silent\'94 side-effects.\
1. Driver-First Execution Model All external capabilities (OS, Unix, package managers, SaaS, DBs, HPC) are modeled as drivers with manifests, constraints, and observability.\
\uc0\u9675  Unix/System Execution and Package & Env operations are first-class drivers, not side-channels.\
2. Governable & Safe Policy Engine and Safety Harness Builder are in the critical path for high-impact actions.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance plane can say \'93no\'94 or \'93not like that\'94 regardless of cognitive sophistication.\
3. Extensible & Composable New drivers, Capsules, Template Packs, workspaces, and Meta-Stack engines integrate via:\
Driver SDK, Capsule manifest schema, Workspace contracts.\
\uc0\u9675  Composition via Workflow\u8594 App Synthesizer, Operator Studio, Cross-Capsule Composer.\
4. Self-Improving Daemons and Meta-Stack capabilities analyze:\
Plan outcomes, Capsule metrics, cost/performance, security events.\
\uc0\u9675  System proposes refactors, Capsule decomposition, environment and policy upgrades.\
5. Offline-Capable, Cloud-Ready Local Mode is offline-first for core features (CIR, ledger, Capsules, local drivers).\
\uc0\u9675  Enterprise Mode scales up the same conceptual model for multi-tenant clusters and regulators.\
6. Plane Separation (Data / Control / Governance) Clear logical boundaries between:\
What exists (data), \'a7 What is done (control), \'a7 What is allowed and sustainable (governance).\
\uc0\u9675  Failure or compromise in one plane must not silently corrupt others.\
7. Model-Provider Agnostic The Model Layer is pluggable:\
GPT-5.1 Pro/Thinking, alternatives, local models.\
\uc0\u9675  Model selection is driven by:\
Policy, data classification, cost and performance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

