\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 2. Planes Architecture: Data, Control & Governance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section formalizes the three primary planes of the OS Dashboard AI Assistant\'97Data Plane, Control Plane, and Governance & Policy Plane\'97and defines how they interlock across Local, Enterprise, and Hybrid deployments. Each plane is a conceptual slice of responsibility, not necessarily a separate deployment tier. The same physical component may participate in multiple planes, but with different roles and guarantees in each. All higher-order behavior (workspaces, driver fabric, capsules, Meta-Stack, HyperMesh) is built as compositions over these planes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 2.1 Data Plane \'96 Definition, Responsibilities & Boundaries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The Data Plane is the system\'92s memory and record of reality. It contains:\
The facts of what exists (projects, documents, code, configurations, environments, twins, capsules, policies).\
\'95 The history of what has happened (ledger events, logs, metrics, traces, policy decisions).\
\'95 The interpreted structure of those facts (CIR, indices, graphs, archives).\
\'95 It does not decide what should happen (that is the Control Plane), nor whether something is allowed or economically\
acceptable (Governance & Policy Plane). It simply records, serves, and indexes. 2.1.1 Purpose & Responsibilities The Data Plane is responsible for:\
\'a0\
\'a0\
Persisting core content and state:\
Projects, tasks, workspaces, Master Stack entries.\
\uc0\u9675  CIR Documents & Blocks (normalized representations of documents, code, notes, logs, research artifacts).\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule manifests, Capsule Packs, Blueprints, My Stack Capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  Digital Twin and Cognitive Twin definitions and state snapshots.\
\uc0\u9675  Policies, Policy Packs, Safety Harnesses, Compliance Packs (as data objects).\
\'95 Persisting temporal & causal records:\
Project Ledger events (append-only, tamper-evident).\
\uc0\u9675  Policy evaluations and governance decisions.\
\uc0\u9675  AI usage and billing events.\
\uc0\u9675  Environment changes (package installs/upgrades/removals, blueprint convergence, drift detections).\
\'95 Persisting observability & telemetry:\
Metrics (time-series).\
\uc0\u9675  Structured logs.\
\uc0\u9675  Traces (cross-component execution paths).\
\'95 Providing query surfaces & indices:\
Full-text search.\
\uc0\u9675  Semantic/vector search.\
\uc0\u9675  Knowledge and dependency graphs.\
\uc0\u9675  Time-series & analytical queries over metrics and events.\
\'95 Supporting time-travel, replay & reconstruction:\
Reconstruct project state and environment \'93as of\'94 a point in time.\
\uc0\u9675  Replay workflows and investigate incidents.\
\uc0\u9675  Provide inputs for research backtesting and Meta-Stack analysis.\
\'95 Key invariant: All durable state that matters to OS Dashboard must be representable inside the Data Plane and reachable\
via structured queries. 2.1.2 Scope & Boundaries In scope:\
Core content & configuration CIRDocuments & CIRBlocks (docs, code, configs, logs elevated to CIR, research notes).\
\uc0\u9675  Project and workspace metadata and settings.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule manifests, tests, environment specs, execution traces.\
\uc0\u9675  Twin definitions, parameters, and state histories.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy & governance definitions and versions.\
\'95 Temporal & causal records\
ProjectEvents in the Ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy evaluation events.\
\uc0\u9675  Usage and billing records.\
\'95 Indices & telemetry\
Full-text indices over CIR, manifests, metadata.\
\uc0\u9675  Vector indices over content, code, logs, twins, capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  Graph indices linking concepts, experiments, capsules, policies, and twins.\
\uc0\u9675  Metrics, logs, traces.\
\'95 Out of scope:\
Purely ephemeral computation state:\
In-process caches, transient prompts, model internal states, short-lived buffers.\
\'95 Live workflow execution state:\
Owned by the Control Plane and reflected into the Data Plane via events, not stored as hidden in-memory mutable state.\
\'95 Change discipline:\
The Data Plane is mutated only via Control Plane actions that have been authorized by Governance.\
\'95 From a human/regulator perspective, the Data Plane is effectively read-only; write operations are always mediated by\
plans, drivers, capsules, and policy.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 2.1.3 Content, CIR, Ledger & Knowledge Stores\
The Data Plane is composed of multiple logical stores. At a minimum:\
CIR & Content Store Stores canonical content in Canonical Internal Representation:\
CIRDocument with metadata and ordered CIRBlocks. \'a7 CIRBlock for paragraphs, code cells, equations, tables, headings, diagrams, annotations, etc.\
\uc0\u9675  Supports:\
Version history, branching, and merge metadata. \'a7 Links back to external sources (Git, SaaS docs, DB snapshots) when applicable. \'a7 Classification tags:\
Sensitivity (public/internal/confidential/PHI/PCI/etc.). \uc0\u9633  Domain/workspace tags. \u9633  Compliance tags. \u9633 \
\uc0\u9675  Used by:\
Cognitive Layer (context assembly and reasoning). \'a7 Workspaces (Dev, Research, Writer, Finance, Cyber, Twins). \'a7 Evidence generators and auditors. 1. Project & Workspace Store Models:\
Projects, Tasks, Workspaces, Master Stack node(s). \'a7 Memberships and role bindings (references to Identity layer). \'a7 Environment Profiles and Blueprint assignments.\
\uc0\u9675  Links:\
From Projects/Tasks to:\
CIR content, \uc0\u9633  Capsules, \u9633  Ledger events, \u9633  Environment specs, \u9633  Twins and policies. \u9633  2. Capsule & Environment Store Stores:\
