\'95 Driver Execution Fabric\
Provides uniform interface for:\
OS drivers (filesystem, processes, UI automation, network).\
\uc0\u9675  System Execution Layer:\
Unix/kernel commands exposed via structured drivers:\
Generic shell.exec or fine-grained wrappers (e.g., driver.git, driver.ffmpeg, driver.kubectl). \uc0\u9633  \'a7 Command steps include:\
Command, args, working dir, environment, time/CPU/RAM limits. \uc0\u9633 \
\uc0\u9675  Package & Environment drivers:\
brew/choco/winget/apt/dnf/pacman. \'a7 pip/conda/poetry/npm/etc.\
\uc0\u9675  SaaS & Data drivers:\
Git hosting, MS Graph, Google APIs, DBs, internal APIs.\
\uc0\u9675  Simulation & Twin drivers:\
HPC schedulers, lab devices, CAD/CAE tools, twin engines.\
\'95 Control Plane responsibilities for drivers:\
Schedule:\
Where and when commands run (local host, bastion, cluster).\
\'95 Enforce:\
Limits (time, resource, concurrency, budgets).\
\uc0\u9675  Policy decisions from Governance.\
\'95 Capture:\
Outputs, exit codes, runtime stats.\
\uc0\u9675  Structured events for the Ledger and Observability.\
\'95 Failure Modes & Recovery (Control Plane view)\
Driver Failure:\
Mark PlanStep failed with structured error metadata.\
\uc0\u9675  Attempt retries with backoff where safe.\
\uc0\u9675  Consider fallback drivers or degraded workflows.\
\'95 Capsule / Workflow Failure:\
Resume from checkpoints.\
\uc0\u9675  Run compensating actions (rollbacks).\
