\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Provide Plan Previews (drivers, commands, env changes, costs, risks).\
Record approvals and overrides as ledger events and Evidence Packs.\
\uc0\u9675  The Control Plane never directly changes the world; it only does so by driving drivers via Capsules, under Governance\
decisions, and with Data Plane recording. 2.2.5 Driver Fabric Architecture (Registry, Discovery, Invocation Router, Contract Testing) Purpose The Driver Fabric is the canonical mediation layer between AI reasoning and real-world execution. It MUST ensure:\
No execution occurs outside governed drivers.\
\uc0\u9675  Every driver invocation is policy-checked, budgeted, and auditable.\
\uc0\u9675  Driver Fabric Components\
Driver Registry:\
Stores driver manifests, versions, capabilities, required scopes, risk tiers, supported environments.\
\uc0\u9675  Capability Discovery:\
Selects drivers based on required capability, target environment, and policy allowlists.\
\uc0\u9675  Invocation Router:\
Normalizes invocation requests, assigns idempotency keys, routes to appropriate runtime adapter, tracks status.\
\uc0\u9675  Contract Testing Harness:\
Validates driver I/O schema conformance, safety harness integration, and replay semantics.\
\uc0\u9675  Secrets & Credentials Broker (integration point):\
Supplies scoped secrets at runtime; secrets are never embedded in plans or logs.\
\uc0\u9675  Runtime Adapter Layer:\
Translates canonical driver calls into OS/CLI/API/service calls, with structured logging.\
\uc0\u9675  Driver Invocation Record (Required Output)\
Each invocation MUST emit a structured record including:\
Driver id/version, requested capability, scopes, actor/tenant/workspace, start/end timestamps, outcome, artifacts, policy decision references.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  2.2.6 Capsule Runtime Architecture (Sandbox Lifecycle, Recording/Replay, Artifact Capture)\
Purpose Capsules are executable, shareable, auditable \'93work units\'94 (workflow + environment). The runtime MUST provide:\
Deterministic execution envelopes where feasible.\
\uc0\u9675  Sandbox isolation with resource limits.\
\uc0\u9675  Full evidence capture and replay hooks.\
\uc0\u9675  Runtime Lifecycle (Canonical)\
Resolve Capsule manifest \uc0\u8594  Resolve dependencies/drivers \u8594  Provision environment \u8594  Run workflow graph \u8594  Capture artifacts/evidence \u8594  Persist run record \u8594  Optional publish/share.\
\uc0\u9675  Sandbox Requirements\
Isolation:\
Container/VM boundary appropriate to risk tier.\
\uc0\u9675  Resource limits:\
CPU/memory/disk/network quotas enforced per policy.\
\uc0\u9675  Recording:\
Command/API transcripts, environment fingerprints, inputs/outputs captured per policy.\
\uc0\u9675  Replay:\
Re-run capability with fixed inputs and pinned dependencies when allowed.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  2.2.7 Asynchronous Execution Fabric (Queues/Topics, Worker Pools, Idempotency, DLQs)\
Purpose Provide a scalable substrate for high-volume execution workloads as growth becomes exponential. Core Requirements Queue semantics:\
At-least-once delivery with idempotency keys and deduplication.\
\uc0\u9675  Priority scheduling:\
Interactive lanes vs batch lanes.\
\uc0\u9675  Backpressure:\
Per-tenant and global concurrency caps; downstream health-aware throttling.\
\uc0\u9675  DLQs:\
Dead-letter routing with operator tooling for inspection and controlled re-drive.\
\uc0\u9675  Worker pools:\
Separate pools for drivers, capsule runs, indexing, evidence generation, and analytics/backfills.\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  2.2.8 Human-in-the-Loop Approval Gates (Review, Multi-Party Approvals, Overrides)\
Principle Approvals MUST be first-class workflow nodes, not ad-hoc UI prompts. Approval Triggers (examples) High-risk driver tiers (filesystem deletes, production deploys, privilege changes).\
\uc0\u9675  Budget threshold exceedance (cost spikes).\
\uc0\u9675  Policy \'93conditional allow\'94 requiring attestation.\
\uc0\u9675  Approval Mechanics\
Single-party or multi-party approvals (configurable by policy).\
\uc0\u9675  Override paths:\
Break-glass approvals MUST be logged, time-bounded, and post-reviewed.\
\uc0\u9675  Plan diffs:\
Approvals SHOULD show \'93plan diff\'94 before/after transformations applied by policy.\
