\cf2 2.3.3 Budgeting, Cost Governance & Billing Hooks\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Governance Plane integrates tightly with the AI Billing & Usage Fabric. Cost Governance & Budgets Policies specify:\
Per-tenant, per-project, per-workspace budgets for:\
Model tokens and calls. \'a7 Driver invocations (e.g., DB queries, HPC jobs, long-running simulations). \'a7 Environment operations (package installs/updates, cluster scale-ups). \'a7 Storage and telemetry retention.\
\'95 Enforce:\
Hard limits (block further actions).\
\uc0\u9675  Soft limits (warnings, approvals, or delayed execution).\
\uc0\u9675  Adaptive routing to:\
Cheaper models for exploratory tasks. \'a7 Slower batch pipelines instead of ad-hoc high-cost workflows.\
\'95 Decision integration\
Before executing high-cost plans:\
Orchestrator obtains:\
Cost envelope and budget state from Billing & Governance. \'a7 Possible alternative (cheaper) plan variants suggested by Billing Optimizer daemons.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance returns:\
ALLOW, DENY, REQUIRE_APPROVAL, or DEFER/SCHEDULE.\
\'95 Approvals for over-budget actions:\
Bound to finance or admin roles.\
\uc0\u9675  Logged as events with justification fields and Evidence Packs.\
\'95 Data Plane & Reporting\
Usage and billing records:\
Written into the Data Plane as first-class entities.\
\uc0\u9675  Used for:\
Dashboards and forecasts. \'a7 Cognitive Economy Engine & Strategy Garden (higher layers). \'a7 Per-Capsule and per-driver cost attribution.\
\'95 Governance thus acts as joint safety, compliance, and economic governor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.3.4 Policy Enforcement Points (PEP/PDP Pattern) & Decision Logging\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Principle Policy must be enforced at multiple layers; it is not sufficient to check policy only at planning time. Required Enforcement Points Edge PEP:\
All user/API requests that can cause execution MUST pass a PEP before reaching the Orchestrator.\
\uc0\u9675  Plan PEP:\
Plans MUST be evaluated and may be transformed (deny/allow/allow-with-conditions) prior to execution.\
\uc0\u9675  Driver Boundary PEP:\
Every driver invocation MUST be checked at invocation time (TOCTOU-safe), using current scopes, budgets, and environment state.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule Runtime PEP:\
Capsule build/run MUST be checked for allowed dependencies, environment privileges, and artifact publishing rules.\
\uc0\u9675  Decision Logging (Canonical)\
Every policy decision MUST produce an immutable decision record linked to:\
The triggering intent/plan/driver invocation.\
\uc0\u9675  The actor/tenant/workspace.\
\uc0\u9675  The effective policy version/rule set.\
\uc0\u9675  The outcome (allow/deny/transform/require-approval).\
\uc0\u9675  This record MUST be queryable by the Record Auditor & Logbook and Regulator Fabric.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.3.5 Budget Enforcement Points & Cost Admission Control\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Budget enforcement MUST occur at:\
Plan time:\
Estimate cost/latency envelope; block or require approval if above threshold.\
\uc0\u9675  Model call time:\
Enforce token/compute budgets; downshift models if allowed.\
\uc0\u9675  Driver invocation time:\
Enforce per-driver and per-tenant quotas; prevent execution storms.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule runtime time:\
Enforce resource budgets for sandbox runs; throttle batch jobs.\
\uc0\u9675  Cost Admission Control (recommended)\
When the system is under load or budgets are constrained, the platform SHOULD:\
Reject non-essential batch work.\
\uc0\u9675  Defer evidence pack generation to background lanes.\
\uc0\u9675  Prefer cached or lower-tier inference for non-critical tasks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 2.4 Cross-Plane Flows & Invariants (How Planes Interlock)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Behavior is constrained by cross-plane invariants that connect Data, Control, and Governance. Every side-effectful action is governed and logged.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
1. Any operation that:\
Modifies CIR, code, configs, envs, or twins. \'a7 Executes commands via System Execution Layer. \'a7 Calls external services or writes to external systems.\
\uc0\u9675  Must:\
Be represented as a Plan/Workflow step in Control Plane. \'a7 Be evaluated by Policy Engine (or fall under explicit allowlist). \'a7 Emit Ledger events (and often telemetry) into Data Plane.\
\uc0\u9675  No direct writes bypass Control Plane.\
Data Plane writes come only from:\
Control Plane actions that were governed.\
\uc0\u9675  Direct DB/file writes by arbitrary components are prohibited (or strictly sandboxed and logged as exceptional).\
2. Planning must be Data-aware and Governance-aware. Plan generation (Cognitive Layer + Orchestrator) uses:\
Data Plane for state and history. \'a7 Governance for constraints and budget envelopes.\
\uc0\u9675  Personas/AIC should avoid proposing plans that are impossible or illegal under the current policy/budget\
environment. 3. Governance decisions are themselves data. Every allow/deny/approval/transform decision:\
Becomes a Ledger event. \'a7 Can be inspected by Record Auditor, Regulator, and Meta-Stack layers.\
\uc0\u9675  Policies are versioned and stored in Data Plane, enabling:\
\'93Why was this allowed then but denied now?\'94 style introspection. 4. Observability spans all three planes. Control Plane:\
Emits metrics/logs/traces.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance Plane:\
Emits metrics/logs/traces for policy evaluations and approvals.\
\uc0\u9675  Data Plane:\
Stores observability and ties it to ledger events and entities.\
\uc0\u9675  Meta-Stack:\
Uses the combined signal for systemic analysis. 5. Least privilege and explicit scope. Control Plane components operate within:\
Explicit driver scopes, policy domains, and data sets.\
\uc0\u9675  Data Plane access is:\
Scoped and filtered by Governance, even for internal daemons.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.4.1 Canonical End-to-End Trace Sequence (Intent \uc0\u8594  Plan \u8594  Policy \u8594  Execution \u8594  Evidence \u8594  Result)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Canonical Sequence (high level) 1) Capture Intent (intent_id) 2) Assemble Context Bundle (context_id) referencing CIR + current environment profile. 3) Generate Plan Graph (plan_id) with explicit steps and required drivers. 4) Policy Evaluation (policy_decision_id) \'96 may transform plan; may require approvals. 5) Budget Reservation (budget_reservation_id) \'96 optional but recommended for enterprise flows. 6) Execute (execution_id):\
- enqueue driver/capsule jobs with idempotency keys,\
- track step state transitions,\
- collect outputs and artifacts.\
7) Evidence Capture (evidence_id):\
- driver transcripts,\
- environment snapshots,\
- model call records (redacted as required),\
- policy decisions.\
8) Commit Ledger Events:\
intent\uc0\u8594 plan\u8594 decision\u8594 execution\u8594 evidence edges MUST be recorded as time-ordered ProjectEvents. 9) Present Result:\
User receives outcome + explanation + \'93what was done\'94 provenance links.\
\'a0\
Trace Completeness Invariant Given any final user-visible result, the system MUST be able to reconstruct:\
Which plan executed, which drivers ran, which policies allowed it, and which artifacts were produced.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.4.2 Regulator/Auditor Evidence Retrieval Flow (Read-Only Inspection)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Principle Regulators/auditors must be able to inspect evidence without the ability to execute actions. Flow 1) Regulator authenticates into Regulator Fabric tenant. 2) Regulator requests evidence bundle by:\
Project, date/time range, incident id, release id, or sampling policy. 3) System returns:\
Evidence Pack(s), linked ledger timeline, policy versions, relevant run records, and reproducibility instructions. 4) Regulator MAY request replay in a controlled sandbox:\
Replay MUST be non-destructive and policy-gated, producing additional evidence. 5) All regulator queries are logged and auditable.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.4.3 Offline-First Sync Flow (Local \uc0\u8596  Enterprise)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Scope Offline-first applies to:\
CIR documents/blocks (with local caching).\
\uc0\u9675  Ledger events (append-only sync with conflict handling).\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule artifacts (selective sync based on policy, size, and relevance).\
\uc0\u9675  Sync Model (recommended)\
Local maintains a local ledger segment; Enterprise maintains canonical tenant ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Sync occurs via:\
Event pull (enterprise\uc0\u8594 local) and event push (local\u8594 enterprise) with signature validation.\
\uc0\u9675  Conflicts are resolved by:\
Policy-defined merge rules (per entity type) + explicit user review when ambiguous.\
\uc0\u9675  Data Minimization\
Local sync MUST obey data residency and confidentiality policies (redaction and selective retrieval).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 2.5 Failure Domains, Isolation Boundaries & Failure Containment Across Planes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Plane separation defines failure domains and containment strategies. 2.5.1 Data Plane Failures Examples:\
DB outage or corruption.\
\'95 Object store unavailability.\
\'95 Search/vector index lag or failure.\
\'95 Metrics/logs backend overload.\
\'95 Effects:\
Control Plane may:\
Lose ability to fetch complete context or write events.\
\'95 Governance Plane may:\
Temporarily lose access to recent usage and policy evaluation logs.\
\'95 Containment & Strategies:\
Enter read-only or degraded mode:\
Bl k d i hi h i k i if l d d di i i b d\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Block destructive or high-risk operations if ledger and audit integrity cannot be guaranteed.\
\uc0\u9675  Allow limited low-risk actions using cached context (configurable).\
\uc0\u9675  Signal:\
Health issues to operators via metrics and alerts.\
\'95 Prevent:\
Silent data corruption by treating inconsistent storage as a blocking condition for sensitive operations.\
\'95 2.5.2 Control Plane Failures\
Examples:\
Orchestrator crash.\
\'95 Workflow engine overload.\
\'95 Daemon scheduler failure.\
\'95 Driver worker pool exhaustion.\
\'95 Effects:\
New plans may not be generated.\
\'95 In-flight workflows may stall or be slowed.\
\'95 Data Plane and Governance remain intact.\
\'95 Containment & Strategies:\
Use idempotent PlanSteps and ledger-based checkpoints:\
On restart, reconstruct state from Data Plane and resume where safe.\
\'95 Apply backpressure and prioritization:\
Throttle non-critical workflows.\
\uc0\u9675  Prioritize incident remediation and critical business flows.\
\'95 Governance may:\
Temporarily restrict initiation of high-risk or expensive plans until Control Plane stabilizes.\
\'95 2.5.3 Governance & Policy Plane Failures / Misconfiguration\
Examples:\
Policy Engine unavailable or degraded.\
\'95 Conflicting policies causing deadlocks or global deny.\
\'95 Misapplied Compliance Pack.\
\'95 Effects:\
Control Plane cannot safely determine allow/deny for new actions.\
\'95 Risk of under- or over-restricted behavior.\
\'95 Containment & Strategies:\
Default behavior:\
Fail-closed for high-risk operations (system execution, package/env changes, data exports, production twin mutations).\
\uc0\u9675  Fail-open or cached-policy for low-risk operations (e.g., read-only, purely local, or tenant-configured exceptions),\
with explicit flags and warnings.\
\'95 Emergency \'93break-glass\'94 policies:\
Allow designated roles to:\
Override or bypass normal policy evaluation for specific actions, \'a7 With mandatory justification, heavy logging, and automatic Evidence Packs.\
\'95 Safe rollout of policy changes:\
Policy simulation/dry-run mode before full enforcement.\
\uc0\u9675  Staged rollout with monitoring for unintended effects.\
\'95 2.5.4 Tenant & Execution Isolation\
Tenant Isolation Data Plane:\
Per-tenant DBs, schemas, or strong row-level isolation.\
\'95 Control Plane:\
Tenant-aware queues, worker pools, and quotas.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Governance:\
Per-tenant policy sets and compliance packs.\
\uc0\u9675  Explicit cross-tenant flows governed and logged.\
\'95 Execution Isolation\
System Execution and Package & Env drivers:\
Prefer execution in containers/sandboxes/bastion hosts.\
\'95 Capsules:\
Namespaced per tenant/project.\
\uc0\u9675  Denied cross-tenant effects unless explicitly federated with strict policies.\
\'95 Meta-Stack operations:\
Scoped explicitly to allowed sets of tenants/projects; cross-tenant operations require explicit Multi-OS/HyperMesh governance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 2.6 Plane-Specific SLAs, SLOs & Scaling Patterns\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Each plane has distinct non-functional requirements. 2.6.1 Data Plane SLAs/SLOs & Scaling Focus: Durability, integrity, queryability. SLOs:\
Write durability: no acknowledged Ledger/CIR writes lost under defined failure conditions.\
\uc0\u9675  Read latency targets:\
CIR & metadata reads. \'a7 Ledger/event queries. \'a7 Search and vector queries.\
\uc0\u9675  Index freshness:\
Max lag between commit and searchability.\
\'95 Scaling:\
Horizontal scaling of:\
Search and vector indices. \'a7 Metrics/logs infrastructure.\
\uc0\u9675  Sharding/partitioning by:\
Tenant, project, or time.\
\uc0\u9675  Tiering:\
Hot vs cold storage for cost control (especially logs/traces).\
\uc0\u9675  DR:\
Multi-region replication, backups, restore procedures.\
\'95 2.6.2 Control Plane SLAs/SLOs & Scaling\
Focus: Responsiveness and throughput. SLOs:\
Plan preview latency:\
Time from intent to plan outline or proposed actions.\
\uc0\u9675  Workflow scheduling latency:\
Time from scheduled trigger to first step execution.\
\uc0\u9675  Reliability:\
Percentage of workflows completed without orchestration-related errors.\
\'95 Scaling:\
Stateless orchestrator and session services:\
Auto-scaled based on request volume.\
\uc0\u9675  Worker pools for Capsules & drivers:\
Separate pools for interactive vs batch vs heavy compute. \'a7 Priority queues (human-interactive > batch; incident remediation > background).\
\uc0\u9675  Tenant isolation:\
Per-tenant quotas and optional dedicated worker pools to avoid noisy neighbors.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 2.6.3 Governance & Policy Plane SLAs/SLOs & Scaling\
Focus: Correctness, consistency, high availability for decisions. SLOs:\
Policy decision latency:\
Upper bound for allow/deny/approval decisions for typical actions.\
\uc0\u9675  Availability:\
High uptime targets (e.g., \uc0\u8805  99.9%) for enterprise/regulatory environments.\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence Pack SLA:\
Time to assemble and return Evidence Packs for requested time windows/workflows.\
\'95 Scaling:\
Stateless policy evaluators:\
Horizontally scaled with cache for low-risk allowlists.\
\uc0\u9675  Strongly consistent configuration:\
Policy and Compliance Pack updates propagate atomically and verifiably.\
\uc0\u9675  Separate capacity for:\
High-volume everyday policy checks. \'a7 Burst workloads (e.g., large approval cycles, regulatory audits).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 2.7 Open Questions / TODOs (Planes Architecture)\
