Central policy service vs regional satellites; how to maintain consistency for critical rules?\
\uc0\u9675  How to safely cache policy decisions for low-risk actions without violating compliance?\
2. Granularity of Policy Checkpoints Per driver call vs per workflow step vs per Capsule type vs per plan.\
\uc0\u9675  Trade-offs between:\
Audit detail/precision. \'a7 Latency and CPU overhead of policy evaluation. 3. Observability as a Fourth Plane Whether to treat Observability as:\
A formal \'93Telemetry Plane\'94 with its own SLAs and governance, or \'a7 A sub-discipline inside the Data Plane with cross-plane consumers.\
\uc0\u9675  How this impacts Meta-Stack capabilities like HyperDaemon and Global Risk Fabric.\
4. Offline & Intermittent Governance (Local & Edge) In offline Local Mode:\
What categories of operations can proceed with cached policies and deferred logging? \'a7 What reconciliation mechanisms exist when connectivity returns?\
\uc0\u9675  How to mark and treat \'93offline decisions\'94 in audits and Evidence Packs?\
5. Command & Environment Policy Granularity Design of practical Safety Harness schemas for:\
Unix/System Execution commands and arguments. \'a7 Package operations and environment changes (per command, per package, per Capsule).\
\uc0\u9675  Balancing:\
Expressiveness for security/compliance teams. \'a7 Usability and maintainability of policy definitions. 6. Data Plane Multi-Model Strategy H l\
\'a0\
\'a0\
7. How strongly to separate:\
Relational, document, vector, graph, and time-series stores.\
\uc0\u9675  When to consolidate vs specialize, given performance, cost, and complexity.\
\uc0\u9675  Multi-OS / HyperMesh Governance\
For workflows spanning multiple OS Dashboard instances:\
How is governance federated? \'a7 Who is the root of trust for cross-org plans? \'a7 What data is shared across instances for audit vs kept strictly local? 8. Backtesting, Replay & Storage Cost How long to retain:\
Raw logs and traces vs aggregated summaries.\
\uc0\u9675  What minimal subset of events is required to reconstruct:\
Plans, env state, Capsule behaviors, and policy paths. 9. Plane-Aware Cost Models How to attribute cost across planes:\
Data Plane (storage, indexing, telemetry). \'a7 Control Plane (compute, scheduling, Capsule execution). \'a7 Governance Plane (policy evaluation, Evidence Pack generation).\
\uc0\u9675  How this attribution informs:\
Product pricing, \'a7 Internal chargeback, \'a7 Cognitive Economy optimization. 10. Meta-Stack Feedback Boundaries How aggressively may Meta-Stack capabilities (ARC, HyperDaemon, Canon of Truth, Ontological Compiler, Global Policy Fabric) be allowed to:\
Propose plane changes vs directly mutate policies, env specs, or plane configuration?\
\uc0\u9675  What additional Governance constraints apply to Meta-Stack actions vs normal automation?\
11. These questions will be refined and resolved in later sections (Driver Fabric, Capsule System & Ledger, Security & Governance, Billing & Usage Fabric, Meta-Stack), and the plane model will remain the architectural backbone they must respect.\
