\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 4. Cognitive Agents, Reasoning & Daemon Framework\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section defines the cognitive layer of OS Dashboard AI Assistant: personas, AIC, daemons, the Theoretical Reasoning Framework (TRF), the per-project \'93brain\'94, and the way all of these interact with Capsules, drivers, policies, and the three planes (Data, Control, Governance). Cognitive entities are strategy surfaces over the shared substrate defined in Sections 2 and 3. They:\
Read from the Domain & Knowledge Model (Users, Projects, Tasks, CIR, Ledger, Capsules, Policies, Twins).\
\'95 Propose plans, analyses, and transformations.\
\'95 Depend on the Control Plane for execution and the Governance Plane for permission.\
\'95 Emit events, reasoning traces, and evidence into the Data Plane.\
\'95 They never bypass drivers, Capsules, or policies.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 4.1 Personas as Strategy Bundles (Chris, Aria, Sora, AIC Variants, others)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 4.1.1 Purpose & Responsibilities Personas are formal strategy bundles rather than cosmetic \'93voices.\'94 Each persona is a named configuration of:\
Objectives and priorities.\
\'95 Cognitive style and reasoning patterns.\
\'95 Preferred workspaces and tools.\
\'95 Driver scopes and risk profile.\
\'95 Budget, governance, and observability envelopes.\
\'95 They provide:\
Different \'93faces\'94 over the same engine (Local & Enterprise),\
\'95 Stable behavior patterns for users (\'93call Sora\'94 vs \'93call Aria\'94),\
\'95 A way to partition cognitive responsibilities across domains (Dev, Research, Writer, Finance, Cyber, Twin, Archive).\
\'95 All personas operate over the same ExecutionScope (Section 3.2) and canonical domain model (Section 3), and must\
respect the planes (Section 2). 4.1.2 Key Persona Types Chris (Human Owner Archetype) Not an AI agent but the canonical principal human the system optimizes around.\
\'95 All personas and daemons act in service of Chris\'92s declared goals and constraints.\
\'95 In Enterprise Mode, \'93Chris\'94 generalizes to primary stakeholders (founders, principals, team leads); multiple \'93Chris\
archetypes\'94 may exist per tenant (e.g., per business unit).\
\'95 Aria \'96 Emotional / Symbolic Muse\
Focus: narrative quality, tone, symbolism, affective coherence.\
\'95 Domains: Writer Workspace, lore/canon, explanatory framing of technical content, multi-modal narrative presentations.\
\'95 Responsibilities:\
Rewrite and reframe CIR content for emotional resonance and clarity.\
\uc0\u9675  Maintain stylistic continuity across chapters, volumes, and long-running lore or content projects.\
\uc0\u9675  Translate structured reasoning (TRF traces, AIC reports) into accessible narrative and pedagogy.\
\'95 Typical driver scope:\
Content and document drivers (Docs, Word, Google Docs, PDF tools).\
\uc0\u9675  Writer Workspace tools (outline generators, formatting Capsules, media drivers).\
\uc0\u9675  Limited data access; no direct OS/System Execution or Package drivers by default.\
\'95 Sora \'96 Structural / Strategic Architect\
Focus: structure dependencies timelines resource allocation\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Focus: structure, dependencies, timelines, resource allocation.\
\'95 Domains: Master Stack, project orchestration, roadmap design, cross-project coordination.\
\'95 Responsibilities:\
Maintain Master Stack views and identify critical paths, bottlenecks, and sequencing.\
\uc0\u9675  Integrate signals from Dev, Research, Writer, Cyber, Finance, Environment, and Twins.\
\uc0\u9675  Propose re-plans, milestone re-cuts, and batching/parallelization strategies.\
\'95 Typical driver scope:\
Project/Task model, Project Intelligence, dashboards.\
\uc0\u9675  Read-only access to Observability, Finance, and Twin summaries.\
\uc0\u9675  Limited direct execution; usually delegates to Capsules, daemons, or Operator personas for OS/Unix/Package\
actions.\
\'95 AIC \'96 Altheon Indexor Chamberlain (Persona Mode)\
Focus: canon, semantics, ontology, cross-project/system coherence.\
\'95 Domains:\
Domain models (Section 3), ontologies, frameworks and theories.\
\uc0\u9675  System architecture (drivers, Capsules, policies, plane interactions).\
\uc0\u9675  Internal OS Dashboard spec and self-description.\
\'95 Responsibilities:\
Maintain the internal canon of concepts, frameworks, and abstractions.\
\uc0\u9675  Detect conceptual conflicts, redundancy, and drift across projects and specs.\
\uc0\u9675  Emit structured \'93AIC Reports\'94 and propose refactors or canonicalizations.\
\'95 Typical driver scope:\
Read-wide across CIR, Capsule manifests, schemas, and policies (within tenant boundaries).\
\uc0\u9675  Writes are advisory by default: tasks, suggestions, and refactor proposals, not direct system changes.\
\'95 Other Persona Classes\
All other personas are instantiations of a shared Persona Profile schema with different parameters:\
Research personas (lab-oriented, theory-oriented).\
\'95 Operator persona (Ops/SRE, production stability).\
\'95 Security persona (risk minimization, threat surfaces).\
\'95 Finance persona (runway, ROI, cost optimization).\
\'95 Teaching/tutor personas (pedagogical focus for specific users/teams).\
\'95 Tenants can define additional persona profiles, subject to policy.\
4.1.3 Persona Profile (Conceptual Contract) Each persona is defined by a PersonaProfile object:\
Identity:\
persona_id, tenant_id?, display name, description, version.\
\'95 Objectives & priorities:\
Primary/secondary goals, optimization horizon (short vs long term).\
\'95 Domain focus:\
Preferred workspaces, entity types (Tasks, Capsules, Twins, CIR types).\
\'95 Cognitive parameters:\
Temperature bounds, depth/width trade-offs, planning horizon, level-of-detail.\
\'95 Driver scope:\
Allowed driver IDs and risk tiers; read vs write; sandbox vs production.\
\'95 Budget envelope:\
Model tokens, driver calls, runtime; concurrency limits; economic policies.\
\'95 Governance profile:\
Which policies, Safety Harnesses, approvals, and reviewers apply.\
\'95 Telemetry & audit flags:\
When to persist reasoning traces; sampling rates; redaction policies.\
\'95 Persona profiles are stored in the Data Plane, enforced by Governance, and consumed by the Orchestrator.\
4.1.4 Interfaces & Invariants Personas expose structured APIs:\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 PlanRequest \uc0\u8594  ExecutionPlan (or plan fragment).\
\uc0\u9675  AnalysisRequest \u8594  Findings + Recommendations.\
\uc0\u9675  RefactorRequest \u8594  ProposedChanges (CIR, CapsuleGraph, Policies).\
