\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 4.2 AIC as Meta-Governor, Canonical Systems Architect & Knowledge Steward\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 4.2.1 Purpose & Responsibilities Beyond its persona surface, AIC is the OS\'92s meta-governor for knowledge and structure:\
Maintains the canon:\
Definitions, frameworks, ontologies, patterns, and system-level invariants.\
\'95 Acts as canonical systems architect:\
Reviews core spec changes, Capsule packs, policy frameworks, environment patterns.\
\'95 Serves as knowledge steward:\
Ensures the ecosystem evolves coherently and does not degenerate into incompatible fragments.\
\'95 AIC is not the Policy Engine (Section 2.3), but it strongly influences policy design and system evolution.\
4.2.2 Key Components (Conceptual) Semantic Indexor Projects CIR blocks, code, Twin models, and Capsule manifests into concept and architecture graphs.\
\uc0\u9675  Maintains rich metadata: domain tags, assumptions, dependencies, lineage.\
\'95 Canon Manager\
Tracks:\
Official definitions and models. \'a7 Deprecated constructs, synonyms, conflicting frameworks.\
\uc0\u9675  Supports:\
Canon queries: \'93What is the canonical definition of X?\'94, \'93Which frameworks implement Y?\'94 \'a7 Canon evolution: promoting/demoting definitions and frameworks.\
\'95 Architecture Overseer\
Watches:\
Architecture docs (CIR), CapsuleGraph, driver catalog, policy schemas. \'a7 Observed behavior via Ledger and Observability.\
\uc0\u9675  Flags:\
Spec vs implementation drift. \'a7 Anti-patterns in Capsule design or driver use. \'a7 Architectural violations (e.g., bypassing Capsules, over-privileged drivers).\
\'95 4.2.3 Data Flows & Contracts\
Inputs CIR (specs, docs, code, research).\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule & Blueprint definitions.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy documents and PolicyPacks.\
\uc0\u9675  Ledger events and Evidence Packs (especially in dev, infra, research, and governance spaces).\
\'95 Analysis\
AIC applies TRF operators (Section 4.6) to:\
Detect conceptual conflicts and redundancies. \'a7 Suggest merges and abstractions across similar Capsules, frameworks, or policies. \'a7 Evaluate consistency between domain models and observed behavior.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Outputs\
AIC Reports:\
CIR documents summarizing findings and recommendations.\
\uc0\u9675  Tasks & Proposals:\
Re-architecture tasks, Capsule refactors, policy changes, ontological updates.\
\uc0\u9675  Canon & Schema Changes:\
Updates to Canon Store, domain schemas, CapsuleGraph structure (subject to human/policy approval).\
\'95 AIC Review Requests\
For major schema, CapsulePack, or policy changes, the Orchestrator can enqueue:\
AICReviewRequest (scope, change_set, risk_level).\
\uc0\u9675  Governance policies may require AIC approval for certain deployments (e.g., production policy packs, Marketplace\
packs).\
\'95 4.2.4 Security & Scope\
In single-tenant or Local Mode:\
AIC may have broad read-access and assume role of \'93internal systems architect.\'94\
\'95 In multi-tenant Enterprise Mode:\
AIC instances are scoped per tenant by default.\
\uc0\u9675  Cross-tenant AIC roles (for Inter-OS Knowledge Network) require explicit opt-in and strict anonymization.\
\'95 AIC changes are:\
Advisory by default.\
\uc0\u9675  Executable only when turned into Capsules or explicit admin actions, passing usual policy checks.\
\'95 4.3 Daemon Families & Roles\
4.3.1 Purpose & Definition Daemons are long-lived or repeatedly scheduled cognitive agents that:\
React to events and periodic checks,\
\'95 Transform telemetry into insights and opportunities,\
\'95 Propose or trigger Capsules and workflows under policy constraints.\
\'95 They extend personas into a continuous, background operating layer.\
4.3.2 Canonical Daemon Families Pattern & Continuity EchoDaemon Detects repeated manual patterns (e.g., series of shell commands, editing steps).\
\uc0\u9675  Proposes Workflow \u8594  App Synthesizer candidates.\
\'95 ArchivistDaemon\
Ensures important artifacts enter Archive / Continuity / Resonance.\
\uc0\u9675  Maintains long-horizon memory and promotes key items to canon.\
\'95 Forecast & Optimization\
OracleDaemon Generates scenario forecasts and \'93possible futures\'94:\
Delivery timelines, risk trajectories, research paths, env health outcomes.\
\uc0\u9675  Feeds Sora, Project Intelligence, Strategy Garden.\
\'95 BillingOptimizerDaemon\
Analyzes UsageRecords and cost patterns.\
\uc0\u9675  Suggests model changes, caching, scheduling, or Capsule refactors to minimize spend.\
\'95 Quality & Critique\
CriticDaemon Reviews code, docs, frameworks, Capsules, and env changes.\
\uc0\u9675  Flags quality issues, missing tests, ambiguous reasoning, anti-patterns.\
\'95 SecurityMonitorDaemon\
