\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 5. Driver Architecture & System Execution Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section defines the Driver Fabric of the OS Dashboard AI Assistant: the governed execution substrate that turns OS capabilities, Unix commands, package managers, SaaS APIs, data systems, research tools, and hardware into typed, auditable capabilities that personas, daemons, AIC, Capsules, and workflows can plan over. Drivers are the only legitimate path from cognition and planning (Sections 2\'964) to real-world side-effects. Everything else in the system is modeling and reasoning; drivers are execution. 5.0 Purpose & Responsibilities Purpose The Driver Architecture provides a uniform, policy-aware substrate for all actions initiated from OS Dashboard, including:\
Local OS operations (filesystem, processes, windows, containers, networking).\
\'95 The System Execution Layer (arbitrary Unix commands and command graphs, local/sandboxed/remote).\
\'95 Package & Environment automation (OS package managers, language package managers, runtime installers).\
\'95 Software / SaaS / Data / Workflow / Governance / Research & Simulation driver calls.\
\'95 Sandbox & Testbed environments for safe experimentation and security analysis.\
\'95 Responsibilities\
Abstract heterogeneous systems behind a common driver contract:\
Capabilities, inputs/outputs, side-effects, risk tier, and cost profile.\
\'95 Enforce governance, identity, cost, and safety at execution time:\
Every call is evaluated against Policy Engine + AI Billing & Usage Fabric.\
\'95 Produce rich telemetry and ledger events for all operations:\
Reproducibility, auditability, postmortems, and cost attribution.\
\'95 Expose driver capabilities for planning-time discovery & estimation:\
AIC, personas, daemons, and Capsules can reason over available capabilities, costs, and risks.\
\'95 Provide scheduling, backpressure, and prioritization:\
Coordinate driver usage across users, personas, daemons, and projects.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 5.1 Driver Taxonomy & Design Principles\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 5.1.1 Driver Taxonomy All drivers are instances of logical capability families, not just \'93tool wrappers.\'94 Core families:\
OS Drivers Filesystem, processes, windows/UI, containers, local networking, notifications.\
\'95 Unix / System Execution Drivers\
Shell commands, binaries, scripts, command graphs; local, sandboxed, or remote.\
\'95 Package & Environment Drivers\
OS package managers (brew/apt/dnf/etc.), language/package managers (pip/conda/poetry/npm/etc.), runtime installers.\
\'95 Hardware Drivers\
GPU/TPU, sensors, lab devices, robots, edge nodes, audio/video, peripherals.\
\'95 Software & SaaS Drivers\
Editors, IDEs, office suites, browsers, ticketing, Git, CI/CD, internal APIs.\
\'95 Data Drivers & Catalogs\
DBs, warehouses, lakes, search indices, logs, telemetry streams.\
\'95 Workflow Drivers\
CI/CD systems, ETL/ELT, schedulers, approval engines, runbook/orchestration tools.\
\'95 Research & Simulation Drivers\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 esea c & S\
u at o e s Scientific runtimes (Python/MATLAB/R/Julia), CAD/CAE/CFD tools, HPC job schedulers, remote labs.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance & Policy Drivers\
Access control, budgets, residency, compliance packs, approval workflows.\
\'95 Sandbox & Testbed Drivers\
Container/VM spawning, isolation, recording and replay.\
\'95 Each driver registers in a Driver Registry with:\
driver_id and version,\
\'95 Capability descriptors (verbs, resource types),\
\'95 Supported scopes (local, sandbox, remote host, cluster),\
\'95 Risk tier (read-only / mutating / privileged),\
\'95 Cost & latency profile,\
\'95 Policy hooks and safety harness references.\
\'95 5.1.2 Design Principles\
Capability-First, Not Tool-First Drivers declare what they can do (capability) before how they do it (CLI/API/SDK).\
\uc0\u9675  e.g., video.thumbnail.generate rather than \'93run ffmpeg with these flags.\'94\
\'95 Uniform Invocation Contract\
Every invocation conceptually uses:\
driver_id, capability, inputs, execution_scope, policy_context, observability_context \uc0\u8594  result | error Where execution_scope always includes an Actor and Project (Section 3.2).\
\'95 Governed by Default\
Every driver call passes:\
Policy Engine (allow/deny/require-approval/transform/log-only). \'a7 AI Billing & Usage Fabric (budgets, quotas, cost estimation).\
\'95 Environment-Aware\
Drivers understand EnvironmentSpecs & Blueprints (Section 3.9, 5.4).\
\uc0\u9675  They must not silently drift machines away from declared manifests; all env changes are explicit and ledgered.\
\'95 Idempotent & Declarative Where Possible\
Drivers declare idempotency and side-effect characteristics.\
\uc0\u9675  Environment-related drivers emphasize declarative convergence (\'93make env match Blueprint X\'94) over ad-hoc\
imperative operations.\
\'95 Auditable & Reproducible\
Every call emits a Ledger event with enough metadata to:\
Reconstruct what happened, \'a7 Replay, backtest, or investigate later.\
\'95 Pluggable & Versioned\
Multiple implementations of the same abstract capability can coexist.\
\uc0\u9675  Selection via policy, cost, performance, and environment constraints.\
\'95 Sandboxable & Testable\
Drivers must support sandbox execution and self-tests.\
\uc0\u9675  High-risk capabilities require sandbox-first patterns and explicit promotion to production.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 5.1.3 Driver Contract Schema Standard (Required Manifest Fields)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Drivers MUST publish a machine-readable contract (manifest) with at least:\
driver_id, version, provider, supported_platforms capabilities (verbs), inputs schema, outputs schema required_scopes (RBAC/ABAC), allowed_resources, residency constraints risk_tier (ReadOnly/Low/Medium/High/Critical) + default approval policy idempotency support (required/optional) + idempotency_key semantics preconditions and postconditions (including safety invariants) telemetry requirements (logs/traces/events) evidence requirements (run record fields, artifacts, redaction rules) cost model (estimated latency, compute, token usage if relevant) dependency list (runtime libs, tools, services) This contract is the basis for:\
Policy evaluation at driver boundary.\
\uc0\u9675  Automated contract testing and certification.\
\uc0\u9675  Deterministic audit and replay tooling.\
\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 5.1.4 Driver Idempotency, Replay & Evidence Requirements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Idempotency All non-read-only drivers SHOULD support idempotency keys. All high-risk drivers MUST support idempotency keys or provide compensating actions.\
\uc0\u9675  Replay\
Drivers SHOULD support replay in controlled sandboxes when feasible. Where replay is not feasible (external side-effects), drivers MUST emit sufficient evidence to validate actions post hoc.\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence\
Every driver invocation MUST produce:\
Structured run record (inputs summary, outputs summary, timing, exit code/outcome).\
\uc0\u9675  Artifact references (files created/modified, logs, diffs, reports).\
\uc0\u9675  Policy decision references (policy ids/versions).\
\'a0\
\uc0\u9675  5.1.5 Driver Risk Tiers & Required Approval Gates (Recommended Default)\
ReadOnly:\
No approval required; bounded by rate limits; full audit.\
\uc0\u9675  Low:\
No approval by default; may require approval under sensitive scopes.\
\uc0\u9675  Medium:\
Approval required for certain tenants/workspaces; plan preview required.\
\uc0\u9675  High:\
Approval required; multi-party approval recommended for enterprise; break-glass allowed with post-review.\
\uc0\u9675  Critical:\
Approval required + restricted to designated roles; requires explicit attestations and enhanced evidence packs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

