\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.1 Logical Storage Model, Data Ownership & Residency\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 6.1.1 Purpose & Responsibilities The storage layer must:\
Provide canonical, queryable storage for all core entities (CIR, Ledger, Capsules, Policies, Usage, Observability).\
\'95 Respect tenant boundaries, ownership, and residency in Enterprise Mode.\
\'95 Support offline-first Local Mode with optional sync into an enterprise cluster.\
\'95 Expose structured, policy-aware APIs to Cognitive and Governance planes.\
\'95 6.1.2 Storage Domains\
Logically, storage is grouped into domains:\
Core Metadata Store Relational DB (SQLite/Postgres) for:\
Users, Tenants, Roles, Policies, Projects, Tasks, Workspaces. \'a7 Capsule metadata, Packs, EnvironmentSpecs/Blueprints, Twins. \'a7 UsageRecords, Cost entities, Driver manifests & Registry. \'a7 Ledger summaries and projections.\
\'95 CIR / Content Store\
Canonical content (CIRDocuments & CIRBlocks).\
\uc0\u9675  Raw source files (docs, PDFs, code, notebooks) when needed.\
\uc0\u9675  Rendered derivatives (HTML, PDFs) where useful.\
\'95 Artifact Store\
Capsule artifacts (scripts, bundles, templates).\
\uc0\u9675  Simulation outputs, compiled binaries, experiment results.\
\uc0\u9675  Container images (via registry) and downloaded models.\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence Packs (packaged ledger + CIR + env snapshots).\
\'95 Observability Stores\
Metrics (time-series DB).\
\uc0\u9675  Logs (structured log store).\
\uc0\u9675  Traces (distributed tracing backend).\
\uc0\u9675  Command outputs and environment snapshots from System Execution & Package drivers.\
\'95 Search / Index Stores\
Full-text indices.\
\uc0\u9675  Semantic / vector indices.\
\uc0\u9675  Knowledge / relation indices (graph overlays).\
\'95 Secrets & Key Stores\
Credentials, API tokens, encryption keys.\
\uc0\u9675  Isolated from application data and heavily governed.\
\'95 6.1.3 Ownership & Residency\
Local Mode Single \'93personal tenant\'94 on a single device.\
\uc0\u9675  Data resides on local filesystem by default (encrypted where supported).\
\uc0\u9675  User is sole owner; any sync/export is explicit and opt-in.\
\'95 Enterprise Mode\
Every record tagged with tenant_id; tenants own their data.\
\uc0\u9675  Strict data partitioning per tenant at DB, index, and object layers.\
\uc0\u9675  Residency tags (e.g., EU_ONLY, US_ONLY, ON_PREM, NO_CLOUD) attached to data and used to:\
Constrain physical storage locations. \'a7 Constrain compute placement (drivers, Capsules, models) at execution time.\
\'95 6.1.4 Interfaces & Contracts\
All write paths (applications, drivers, Capsules, daemons) must go through Domain APIs which:\
Attach: tenant_id, project_id, classification, residency, lineage.\
\uc0\u9675  Emit Ledger events for significant changes.\
\'95 Consistency expectations:\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 y\
p Strong / transactional for critical metadata (policies, identity, billing, environment specs).\
\uc0\u9675  Eventual for large content and derived indices (search, embeddings, analytics).\
\uc0\u9675  6.1.5 Implementation Notes & Trade-offs\
Local Mode:\
Typically SQLite + filesystem; lightweight full-text index; optional simple vector index.\
\'95 Enterprise Mode:\
Postgres (or equivalent) for metadata & ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Object storage for content and artifacts.\
\uc0\u9675  Dedicated clusters for search/vector/observability per region or tenant tier.\
\'95 Residency is enforced at:\
Provisioning time (per-region clusters), and\
\uc0\u9675  Access time (policy checks and routing).\
