\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.10 Evidence Store & Replay Artifacts (Reproducibility Envelope)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Purpose Provide durable, queryable storage for execution evidence and reproducibility artifacts across:\
Driver invocations.\
\uc0\u9675  Capsule runs.\
\uc0\u9675  Model calls (subject to redaction and residency policy).\
\uc0\u9675  Core Evidence Object Types (recommended)\
RunRecord:\
Canonical record for any driver/capsule run (ids, timestamps, actor/tenant, outcome, metrics).\
\uc0\u9675  Transcript:\
Command/API call transcripts, structured and searchable.\
\uc0\u9675  ArtifactBundle:\
Pointers to produced artifacts (files, diffs, reports, binary outputs).\
\uc0\u9675  EnvironmentSnapshot:\
Pinned dependency graph + environment fingerprints for replay.\
\uc0\u9675  PolicyDecisionRecord:\
Immutable policy decision + conditions + effective policy version.\
\uc0\u9675  ModelCallRecord:\
Provider/model id, token counts, latency, redaction summary, routing decision references.\
\uc0\u9675  Integrity & Linkage Requirements\
Evidence objects MUST be content-addressed or integrity-protected (hashes).\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence objects MUST be linked into the Ledger (6.3) as ProjectEvents, enabling timeline reconstruction.\
\uc0\u9675  Retention MUST be policy-driven (legal hold, regulator requirements, tenant settings).\
\uc0\u9675  Security Requirements\
Evidence MUST be encrypted at rest and in transit.\
\uc0\u9675  Access MUST be mediated by RBAC/ABAC and Regulator Fabric rules.\
\uc0\u9675  Redaction/tokenization MUST be applied per policy prior to storage when required.\
\uc0\u9675  Replay Guarantees\
Replay MUST be possible at least at the \'93explainability replay\'94 level:\
Given evidence, the system can show what happened even if a full re-run is not feasible.\
