\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 8. Capsule System, Project Ledger & Workflow Synthesis / Automation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section defines the execution grammar of OS Dashboard \'96 how work is encoded, governed, executed, and remembered:\
Capsule System \'96 executable, inspectable, shareable workflows.\
\'95 Project Ledger \'96 tamper-evident, queryable history of actions, environments, and decisions.\
\'95 Workflow Synthesis & Automation \'96 recording real activity (UI + CLI + driver calls) and turning it into reusable\
Capsules and apps.\
\'95 Capsules + Ledger sit at the intersection of all three planes:\
Data Plane \'96 code, parameters, artifacts, results, and evidence.\
\'95 Control Plane \'96 orchestration of drivers, tasks, and workflows.\
\'95 Governance Plane \'96 policies, safety harnesses, approvals, auditability.\
\'95 They are also the primary substrate for higher tiers (Meta-Stack, Reality Twin Mesh, Self-Evolving Capsule Ecosystem, etc.),\
which operate over encoded workflows, twins, and histories.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 8.1 Capsule Taxonomy (Template, Analytical, Executable, Infra, Composite, Test)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 8.1.1 Purpose / Responsibilities Define a minimal but expressive set of Capsule kinds so that:\
Planning, governance, and marketplace behavior can specialize by type.\
\'95 Users, personas, and daemons can reason about what a Capsule is allowed to do and what it is expected to produce.\
\'95 Risk, review, and sandboxing policies can be tuned per type.\
\'95 8.1.2 Core Capsule Types\
Template Capsules Non- or lightly-executable scaffolds.\
\uc0\u9675  Capture reusable patterns: task frames, workflow skeletons, doc structures.\
\uc0\u9675  Examples: \'93Standard PR Review Flow\'94, \'93Experiment Design Template\'94, \'93Narrative Outline Template\'94.\
\uc0\u9675  Typically instantiated into Executable/Analytical Capsules per project.\
1. Analytical Capsules Read-heavy analytics, simulation, and reporting workflows.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
2. Use Data / Research / Simulation / SaaS drivers and System Execution in read mode.\
\uc0\u9675  Outputs: dashboards, reports, derived datasets, CIR documents, metrics.\
\uc0\u9675  Side-effects limited to new artifacts and CIR updates (no infra writes).\
\uc0\u9675  Executable Capsules\
General automation with write side-effects.\
\uc0\u9675  May invoke OS, Unix, Package & Env, SaaS, Data, and Workflow drivers.\
\uc0\u9675  Used for: builds, migrations, reconciliations, content generation, routine operations.\
\uc0\u9675  Require full policy evaluation, sandboxing as appropriate, and complete audit logging.\
3. Infra Capsules Specialized subclass of Executable Capsules with explicit infra-changing semantics:\
Deploy services, roll back releases, patch servers, rotate secrets, modify firewall rules, scale clusters.\
\uc0\u9675  Strongest safety, approval, and Evidence Pack requirements.\
\uc0\u9675  Typically run from Operator, SRE, or Cyber workspaces.\
4. Composite Capsules \'93Capsule-of-Capsules\'94 (meta-Capsules).\
\uc0\u9675  Compose other Capsules into graphs:\
Sequential, parallel, conditional, event-driven, sagas with compensating steps.\
\uc0\u9675  Side-effects occur only via constituent Capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  Primary vehicle for cross-workspace orchestration.\
5. Test Capsules Validation flows that assert properties of systems, models, environments, or other Capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  Examples: unit/integration tests, smoke tests, env/driver self-checks, compliance tests.\
\uc0\u9675  Often paired 1:N with Executable/Infra Capsules (pre- and post-conditions).\
6. 8.1.3 Governance & Marketplace Integration Each Capsule declares a single primary type plus optional domain tags (security, finance, research, etc.).\
\'95 Governance and Marketplace use type + tags to determine:\
Required review steps and approvers.\
\uc0\u9675  Allowed scopes (e.g., Infra Capsules disabled in certain tenants/environments).\
\uc0\u9675  Default sandbox level and policy packs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 8.2 Capsule Structure, Metadata, Tests & Constraints\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 8.2.1 Purpose Define a canonical structure for Capsules so the platform can:\
Analyze and govern them statically.\
\'95 Execute them deterministically.\
\'95 Render and edit them across tools.\
\'95 Integrate them with Ledger, Evidence Packs, and Meta-Stack.\
\'95 8.2.2 Core Structure (Conceptual Schema)\
Every Capsule version includes at least:\
Identity & Classification capsule_id (stable UUID), version (semver), primary type (8.1).\
\uc0\u9675  Name, description, domain tags (Dev, Research, Writer, Finance, Cyber, SRE, Twin, etc.).\
\uc0\u9675  Owner(s), tenant, creation/update timestamps.\
\uc0\u9675  Visibility scope: private, project, team, tenant, marketplace.\
\'95 Interface Definition\
Inputs: parameters with types, defaults, validation constraints, and hints (e.g., \'93path to dataset\'94, \'93env name\'94).\
\uc0\u9675  Outputs: result types (CIR docs, artifacts, metrics, status objects), plus primary artifacts for indexing.\
\uc0\u9675  Pre-conditions: predicates over environment, data, or state that must be true before running.\
\uc0\u9675  Post-conditions: invariants expected after completion (e.g., tests passing, health checks green).\
\'95 Execution Plan Stub\
High-level step graph (DAG): steps refer to driver capabilities and/or sub-Capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  No raw free-form shell inside the manifest:\
Shell/CLI logic is wrapped through driver declarations (e.g., unix.exec with structured arguments).\
\'95 Environment & Dependencies\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Environment & Dependencies\
Reference to one or more Environment Specs / Blueprints (8.3, 8.12).\
\uc0\u9675  Required driver capabilities (Git, DB, MATLAB, CAD, CI/CD, etc.).\
\uc0\u9675  Supported OS families and constraints.\
\'95 Tests & Checks\
Linked Test Capsules for:\
Unit, integration, regression, env sanity.\
\uc0\u9675  Embedded checks:\
Post-run assertions (e.g., \'93CI pipeline green\'94, \'93no 5xx in last N minutes\'94).\
\'95 Governance Metadata\
Risk tier (read-only, write, infra-admin).\
\uc0\u9675  Required approver roles and quorum (e.g., Security Reviewer + SRE Lead).\
\uc0\u9675  Required policy packs (e.g., \'93Prod Infra Ops\'94, \'93PII-Safe Reporting\'94).\
\uc0\u9675  Evidence Pack requirements and templates (8.17).\
\'95 Observability Hooks\
Metrics to emit.\
\uc0\u9675  Logging level and redaction rules (PII/PHI/IP, classification).\
\uc0\u9675  Trace correlation behavior (span/link to Ledger events).\
\'95 8.2.3 Constraints\
Capsule manifests are declarative and statically analyzable:\
Drivers, potential resources, and approximate risk can be inferred before runtime.\
\'95 Imperative logic lives inside:\
Driver implementations, scripts referenced via driver wrappers, or sub-Capsules.\
\'95 A Capsule must be validatable against:\
Schema, dependency resolution, policy packs, and environment specs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

