\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 9.1 Extensibility Principles, Safety Constraints & Trust Model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Purpose Define the rules by which internal and external contributors extend OS Dashboard without compromising safety, governance, or coherence. Core Principles Driver-first abstraction All external systems (apps, CLIs, APIs, infra, data) are surfaced as drivers with manifests.\
\uc0\u9675  Plugins and Capsules orchestrate drivers; they never bypass the Driver Fabric with ad-hoc network or OS calls.\
1. Manifest-driven, policy-aware Every extension (driver, plugin, Capsule, pack, edition) ships with a declarative manifest:\
Capabilities, dependencies, environment specs. \'a7 Risk classification and required policy packs. \'a7 Pricing and licensing metadata (when applicable).\
\uc0\u9675  Policy Engine and Billing Fabric consume manifests for enforcement and metering.\
2. Least privilege & scoped access Extensions run with explicitly declared data scopes, driver scopes, network scopes, and budget scopes.\
\uc0\u9675  The Governance Plane enforces scopes at runtime; no \'93ambient authority\'94.\
3. Multi-tier trust Trust tiers determine default permissions, review depth, and installability:\
Core / Tier-0 \'96 first-party, bundled with platform. \'a7 Verified / Tier-1 \'96 certified third-party (deep review + tests).\
\'a0\
\'a0\
4. Marketplace / Tier-2 \'96 reviewed but not fully certified (restricted scopes). \'a7 Local / Tier-3 \'96 personal/org-internal, dev/experimental (heavily sandboxed, tenant-scoped). \'a7 Tenants and regulators can further restrict allowed tiers.\
\uc0\u9675  Stable contracts, evolvable internals\
Public SDKs, driver contracts, and manifest schemas are strongly versioned.\
\uc0\u9675  Extensions may evolve internally, but breaking contract changes require new major versions and migration paths.\
5. Offline-aware Local Mode must support offline installation from signed bundles.\
\uc0\u9675  Enterprise tenants may run fully private app stores, optionally mirroring a subset of the public Marketplace.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 9.2 Plugin Runtime & Sandbox Model (Permissions, Scopes, Isolation)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Purpose Provide a controlled execution environment for code extensions (plugins) while forcing all side-effects through governed drivers. Plugin Types UI plugins \'96 panels, visualizers, custom workspace views, dashboard widgets.\
\'95 Logic plugins \'96 pure computation, formatting, domain rules, light transformations.\
\'95 Integration plugins \'96 thin shims around external APIs; conceptually realized as drivers.\
\'95 Execution Model\
Out-of-process by default:\
Plugins run in separate processes or containers per tenant or per extension.\
\uc0\u9675  All OS, filesystem, network, and driver access goes through the platform\'92s Execution Proxy.\
\'95 In-process plugins:\
Restricted to pure computation and formatting (no I/O or external calls).\
\uc0\u9675  Primarily for UI composition and minor logic.\
