\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 10.1.1 Primary Threats Compromise of agentic automation Malicious / misaligned Capsules, plugins, drivers, or daemons issuing destructive or exfiltrating commands.\
\uc0\u9675  Prompt injection and data poisoning steering models into unsafe plans.\
\uc0\u9675  Over-entitled agents or personas (Sora, Aria, AIC variants) operating outside intended scopes.\
1. Account / credential compromise Stolen user credentials, SSO tokens, API keys, or service account secrets.\
\uc0\u9675  Session hijacking and token replay.\
2. Supply-chain & extension risk Malicious or vulnerable drivers, plugins, containers, and third-party Capsules.\
\uc0\u9675  Compromised dependencies in Package & Env Drivers (npm/pip/brew/apt/etc.).\
3. Data exfiltration & privacy violation Sensitive content (PII/PHI/PCI/IP/trade secrets) leaving permitted domains.\
\uc0\u9675  Unsafe exports to external LLM providers, SaaS tools, or HyperMesh partners.\
4. Abuse of elevated OS / infra privileges\
\'a0\
\'a0\
5. p g Unbounded use of root/sudo, filesystem writes, kernel-level tools.\
\uc0\u9675  Risky commands via System Execution Layer (rm, dd, iptables, kubectl, ssh, DB CLIs).\
\uc0\u9675  Uncontrolled package/environment changes.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance failure & misconfiguration\
Policies that are too permissive or too restrictive.\
\uc0\u9675  Inconsistent roles, packs, or Safety Harness settings leading to violations or outages.\
6. Insider threat Malicious or negligent insiders misusing powerful automations or regulator views.\
\uc0\u9675  Abusing Law-of-the-OS / policy change privileges.\
7. Systemic & cross-org risk Cascading failures in Capsule graphs.\
\uc0\u9675  Misconfigured HyperMesh / HyperSymphony flows causing multi-tenant impact.\
8. 10.1.2 Security Objectives Least privilege by design For users, agents, Capsules, drivers, plugins, and workflows.\
\uc0\u9675  Minimal required scopes for data, drivers, network, and budgets.\
\'95 Strong isolation\
Hard isolation between tenants.\
\uc0\u9675  Scoped isolation between projects, environments, and sandboxes.\
\'95 End-to-end auditability\
Every impactful operation\'97from intent to model to Capsule to driver to OS\'97is logged and reconstructible in Ledger + Record Auditor.\
\'95 Defense-in-depth\
Identity, auth, policy, Safety Harness, sandboxing, monitoring, and supply-chain controls stacked together.\
\'95 Governed autonomy\
Agents can act autonomously only inside clearly bounded, policy-reviewable envelopes.\
\'95 Regulator-grade transparency\
Enterprise Mode must support regulator tenants with read-only but deep inspection and replay capability.\
\'95 10.1.3 Risk Appetite\
Very low tolerance for:\
Cross-tenant data leakage.\
\uc0\u9675  Unlogged OS/Unix/Package & Env operations.\
\uc0\u9675  Irreversible destructive operations without explicit approval.\
\uc0\u9675  Violations of enabled Compliance Packs (GDPR, HIPAA, SOX, PCI-DSS, EU AI Act, etc.).\
\'95 Moderate tolerance for:\
Overhead from policy checks, logging, and sandboxing.\
\uc0\u9675  Strict defaults requiring explicit relaxation by admins.\
\'95 Configurable per tenant\
Preset baselines (e.g., Regulated, Enterprise, Lab/Research) change:\
Safety Harness defaults, \'a7 Approval thresholds, \'a7 External integration and federation rules.\
