\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 Core Invariant No Unix command or Package/Env change may occur outside the control of the Policy Engine, Safety Harness, sandboxing, and Ledger. Execution Flow Workflow / Capsule defines a step using System Execution or Package & Env driver. 1. Orchestrator builds a Command Intent:\
Actor, Capsule, target env, command, arguments, justification/context. 2. Policy Engine + Safety Harness evaluate:\
Command allowlist, argument/path constraints, env type, classification, budgets.\
\uc0\u9675  Decide: ALLOW, WARN, REQUIRE_APPROVAL, REQUIRE_SANDBOX, DENY.\
3. If allowed:\
Sandbox Manager executes:\
In container/VM/chroot with constrained user, network, filesystem. \'a7 With resource limits (CPU, memory, runtime).\
\uc0\u9675  Outputs (stdout/stderr, exit codes) are structured and logged.\
4. Ledger & Record Auditor:\
Record each step as events with full context (forensics, replay, evidence). 5. Package & Env operations Same flow, plus:\
Dependency resolution and risk checks.\
\uc0\u9675  Drift tracking: before/after snapshots attached to env health metrics.\
\uc0\u9675  Additional checks from Compliance Packs (e.g., no kernel changes in prod without formal approval).\
