\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 12.9 Resilience of Unix/System Execution & Package/Env Drivers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 12.9.1 Isolation & Resource Control Unix/System Execution:\
Commands executed in:\
Containers/VMs or restricted OS accounts where possible, \'a7 With CPU, memory, IO, and runtime limits.\
\uc0\u9675  Network access governed by Safety Harness and policy.\
\'95 Package & Env Drivers:\
Run under restricted service accounts,\
\uc0\u9675  Environment mutations are controlled and auditable,\
\uc0\u9675  Only one package manager operation per host at a time (or tightly limited concurrency) to avoid DB lock issues.\
\'95 12.9.2 Failure Handling\
For SystemExec commands:\
Strict timeouts, non-zero exit codes fully logged.\
\uc0\u9675  Outputs (stdout/stderr) stored or digested as evidence.\
\uc0\u9675  Failures categorized as:\
Command not found, \'a7 Permission denied, \'a7 Resource timeout, \'a7 Policy-blocked,\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 y\
, Unexpected error. \'a7 For Package/Env operations:\
Detect and flag:\
Partial upgrades, lock contention, inconsistent dependency states.\
\uc0\u9675  Environments labeled:\
healthy, converging, degraded, broken.\
\uc0\u9675  Guided remediation Capsules offered for degraded/broken states.\
\'95 12.9.3 Host-Level Safety\
OS Dashboard must not jeopardize host stability:\
Limit number of concurrent commands per host.\
\uc0\u9675  Prioritize host critical services over Dashboard workloads.\
\uc0\u9675  Provide per-host and per-tenant emergency kill-switch to:\
Halt all automation involving SystemExec and Package/Env drivers.\
