\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 12.10.1 Workload Characterization Jobs are:\
Long-running, CPU/GPU or IO intensive,\
\uc0\u9675  Often executed on external HPC clusters, cloud GPU fleets, or specialized lab hardware.\
\'95 12.10.2 Scheduling & Queuing\
Use drivers to integrate with:\
Slurm, Kubernetes, proprietary HPC schedulers, CAD automation APIs, lab systems.\
\'95 Jobs modeled as:\
Asynchronous Capsule steps with:\
Job IDs, queue time, run time, \'a7 Status (queued/running/completed/failed).\
\'95 Concurrency and job limits:\
Configurable per tenant; enforced to avoid overloading shared clusters.\
\'95 12.10.3 Data Handling & Locality\
Large result sets:\
Streamed directly into object storage; avoid funneling through API frontends.\
\'95 Data locality:\
Prefer compute near data; design pipelines to minimize cross-region transfer.\
\'95 12.10.4 Performance & Reliability Metrics\
Measure:\
Queue wait times, job runtime distributions, success rates,\
\uc0\u9675  Cost per job or per simulation campaign.\
\'95 Reliability:\
Idempotent submission and monitoring,\
\uc0\u9675  Robust across intermittent connectivity,\
\uc0\u9675  Checkpointing where supported to resume long jobs after failures.\
\'95 Research Workspace:\
Provides dashboards, progress views, and per-campaign Evidence Pack hooks.\
