\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 13.5.1 Service-to-Service Authentication, mTLS & Service Mesh Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Requirement Enterprise deployments MUST support authenticated, authorized service-to-service communication. Recommended Baseline mTLS between internal services.\
\uc0\u9675  Service identities (SPIFFE/SVID or equivalent) bound to workload identity.\
\uc0\u9675  Central policy for inter-service access (least privilege).\
\uc0\u9675  Service Mesh (optional)\
A service mesh MAY be adopted if it provides:\
mTLS automation, traffic shaping, retries/timeouts, and observability improvements without materially increasing operational risk.\
\uc0\u9675  If not adopting a full mesh, the platform MUST still implement:\
mTLS, standardized retries/timeouts, and consistent tracing headers.\
\uc0\u9675  Network Zones (Enterprise / Hybrid)\
Public Edge Zone API gateways / load balancers.\
\uc0\u9675  Accepts only TLS/HTTPS.\
\uc0\u9675  WAF, DDoS protection, coarse rate-limits.\
1. Application Zone Orchestrator, workspace services, Capsule service, Billing, driver gateways.\
\uc0\u9675  Limited outward access to Data, Governance, and Driver zones.\
2. Governance Zone Policy Engine, Regulator Fabric, Law-of-the-OS, identity sync services.\
\uc0\u9675  Hardened, least-privilege access to all other zones.\
3. Data Zone DBs, object storage endpoints, search/vector clusters, metrics/logs.\
\uc0\u9675  No direct public access.\
4. Driver / Runner Zone System Execution workers, Package & Env runners, HPC gateways, SaaS connectors.\
\uc0\u9675  Network egress tightly controlled per driver type and tenant.\
5. Edge / Agent Zone On-prem and edge agents.\
\uc0\u9675  Communicate outwards to specific ingress endpoints; no inbound routes required.\
6. Zero-Trust Principles All inter-service communication:\
Authenticated (mTLS, service identities).\
\uc0\u9675  Authorized (policy-aware, per-service ACLs).\
\uc0\u9675  Logged for audit.\
\'95 No implicit trust based on network location:\
Segmentation supports containment but policy is primary.\
\'95 Failure Modes & Recovery\
Misconfigured network policies:\
Observability surfaces unexpected service connectivity failures.\
\uc0\u9675  System shifts into \'93plan-only / limited execution\'94 modes for drivers behind blocked routes.\
\'95 Compromised agent:\
Agent identity revoked; traffic blocked; environment isolated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

