\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf4 14. Failure Modes, Risk & Resilience\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 This section defines how the OS Dashboard AI Assistant anticipates, detects, contains, and recovers from failures across:\
Planes: Data, Control, Governance\
\'95 Layers: Presentation/UX, Cognitive, Domain, Driver, Infra\
\'95 Deployment modes: Local, Cloud/Enterprise, Hybrid, Edge\
\'95 The goal is not \'93no failures,\'94 but:\
Predictable, explainable, bounded failures with clear recovery paths, preserved integrity, and regulator-grade evidence. Everything in this section is wired into:\
Observability & Audit (Section 11)\
\'95 Security, Policy & Governance (Section 10)\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 y,\
y ( ) Performance & Reliability (Section 12)\
\'95 Deployment & DR (Section 13)\
\'95 Meta-Stack & HyperDaemon / Law-of-the-OS (Section 17)\
\'95 14.0 Principles & Objectives\
Principles Fail visibly, not silently No critical failure should be invisible to users, operators, or regulators. 1. Fail bounded, not catastrophically Scope and blast radius are constrained by design (per tenant, project, environment). 2. Fail explainably, not mysteriously Every material failure must be reconstructable via Ledger, Logbook, and Evidence Packs. 3. Fail forward Incidents become structured inputs into policy, Capsule design, and systemic-risk learning (HyperDaemon, Law-of-the-OS). 4. Objectives Provide a shared taxonomy for failures.\
\'95 Provide early-warning detection and risk scoring.\
\'95 Codify recovery strategies as Capsules and playbooks, not ad-hoc scripts.\
\'95 Protect CIR, Ledger, Capsule integrity, and evidence.\
\'95 Enable BC/DR with measurable RPO/RTO bounds.\
\'95 Surface systemic risk to HyperDaemon and regulators.\
\'95 14.1 Failure Taxonomy (Data, Control, Driver, Governance, UX, Cognitive, Systemic)\
14.1.1 Classification Axes Every failure is tagged along these dimensions:\
Plane Data Plane \'96 storage, indices, CIR, Ledger, artifacts.\
\uc0\u9675  Control Plane \'96 orchestrator, workflow engine, queues, daemons, drivers.\
\uc0\u9675  Governance Plane \'96 identity, policy engine, Regulator Fabric, Law-of-the-OS.\
\'95 Layer\
Driver & Execution \'96 OS, Unix, Package & Env, SaaS, Data, Research/HPC.\
\uc0\u9675  Application/Domain \'96 workspaces, Capsule runtime, workspace controllers.\
\uc0\u9675  Cognitive \'96 personas, daemons, TRF, planning and reasoning.\
\uc0\u9675  UX / Presentation \'96 UI, API, interaction flows.\
\'95 Scope\
Local (single task or Capsule),\
\uc0\u9675  Project,\
\uc0\u9675  Tenant,\
\uc0\u9675  Cluster / Region,\
\uc0\u9675  Cross-OS / Federation.\
\'95 Severity\
SEV-1 (Critical) \'96 data loss, major outage, regulatory risk.\
\uc0\u9675  SEV-2 (High) \'96 strong user impact, degraded critical functions.\
\uc0\u9675  SEV-3 (Medium) \'96 localized, recoverable without major business impact.\
\uc0\u9675  SEV-4/5 (Low/Informational) \'96 minor glitches, cosmetic issues, near-misses.\
\'95 Root-Cause Category\
Resource exhaustion (CPU, RAM, disk, GPU, file handles).\
\uc0\u9675  Dependency failure (provider, DB, cluster, network).\
\uc0\u9675  Data corruption / inconsistency.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy misconfiguration (too strict / too permissive).\
\uc0\u9675  Misuse / abuse (malicious or negligent).\
\uc0\u9675  Cognitive misreasoning or misalignment.\
\uc0\u9675  UX/interaction mismatch.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 14.1.2 Data Plane Failures\
Storage unavailability DB or object store outages (Postgres/S3/local FS).\
\uc0\u9675  Search/vector index nodes offline.\
\'95 Data corruption / inconsistency\
Partial writes, schema mismatches, broken foreign keys.\
\uc0\u9675  Indexes out of sync with CIR or Ledger.\
\uc0\u9675  Broken Capsule manifests or env specs.\
\'95 Data loss / truncation\
Misconfigured retention or incomplete backups.\
\uc0\u9675  Accidental or malicious deletion.\
\'95 Classification / residency violations\
Data stored in wrong region, bucket, or encryption state.\
\'95 14.1.3 Control Plane Failures\
Planner / orchestrator failures AIC/persona unable to produce valid plan.\
\uc0\u9675  Plans that cannot be executed (no drivers, conflicting constraints).\
\uc0\u9675  Model provider outages impacting planning.\
\'95 Workflow engine failures\
Hung workflows, stuck state transitions, mis-sequenced Capsule steps.\
\uc0\u9675  Deadlocks or livelocks in complex automation graphs.\
\'95 Daemon / scheduler failures\
Daemons not running, over-triggered, or starved.\
\uc0\u9675  Duplicate or conflicting daemons acting on same project.\
\'95 14.1.4 Driver & Execution Failures\
Driver unavailability SaaS/API outages, OS/FS driver errors, unreachable DBs, HPC schedulers down.\
\'95 Driver misconfiguration\
Bad credentials, wrong endpoints, missing permissions, wrong tenant context.\
\'95 System Execution Layer failures\
Non-zero exit codes, timeouts, sandbox violations, resource limit breaches.\
\'95 Package & Env driver failures\
Failed installs/upgrades, half-applied changes, broken package DB, env drift.\
\'95 Edge/agent failures\
Agents offline, out of date, or mis-registered.\
\'95 14.1.5 Governance & Policy Failures\
Over-restrictive policies Legitimate operations blocked, leading to productivity loss.\
\'95 Under-restrictive / missing policies\
Dangerous operations allowed, potential breaches/regulatory issues.\
\'95 Conflicting policies\
Multiple policies producing contradictory decisions (deadlock, inconsistent behavior).\
\'95 Regulator Fabric failures\
Evidence Packs cannot be generated or served.\
\uc0\u9675  Attestations invalid or missing.\
\'95 Law-of-the-OS breakdowns\
Inability to adjudicate disputes due to missing or ambiguous rules.\
\'95 14.1.6 UX & Interaction Failures\
Mi h d i\
\'a0\
\'a0\
Mismatched expectations Users believe an action is safe or small in scope when it is large or risky.\
\'95 Silent or opaque failures\
Errors not surfaced or surfaced without actionable guidance.\
\'95 Alert overload\
Too many low-value alerts; users begin ignoring real issues.\
\'95 Collisions with automation\
Users editing resources while Capsules simultaneously act on them, leading to confusion or conflicts.\
\'95 14.1.7 Cognitive, Meta-Stack & Systemic Failures\
Cognitive & Model-level Hallucination or fabrication in plans/explanations.\
\uc0\u9675  Goal misalignment (local optimization vs tenant goals).\
\uc0\u9675  Temporal incoherence (ignoring important history/archive).\
\uc0\u9675  Cross-persona conflict (e.g., Sora vs Aria vs AIC producing incompatible strategies).\
\'95 Systemic & Meta-Stack\
Cascading failures via capsule networks or HyperMesh.\
\uc0\u9675  Emergent fragility in HyperFoundry or HyperSymphony automation.\
\uc0\u9675  Cross-OS federation failures (inconsistent assumptions between OS instances).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

