\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 17.1 Layering Model Overview, Dependencies & Cross-Layer Invariants\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 17.1.1 Purpose The layering model:\
Provides a map of capability strata from \'93single-user OS\'94 to \'93civilizational governance fabric\'94.\
\'95 Encodes explicit dependencies between capabilities (e.g., ARC requires Capsules + Research Orchestrator + Archive).\
\'95 Ensures that governance and safety strengthen as power increases.\
\'95 Serves as a roadmap for phased implementation and commercialization.\
\'95 17.1.2 Layer Definitions (Summary)\
Layer 1 \'96 Core Per-user / per-org OS. Master Stack, Workspaces, Capsules, Drivers, Policies, Billing, Ledger, Archive.\
\'95 Layer 2 \'96 Advanced\
Unified Research, Simulation, CAD/CAE, Digital Twins, cross-domain simulation, policy sandboxing.\
\'95 Layer 3 \'96 Super\
Meta-systems that reason over projects, Capsules, policies, and knowledge markets (ARC, Theory Engine, Self-Evolving Capsules Knowledge Market Agentic Enterprise Twin)\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Capsules, Knowledge Market, Agentic Enterprise Twin).\
Layer 4 \'96 Hyper Inter-OS and ecosystem-scale orchestration (HyperMesh, HyperLab, HyperRegent, HyperSymphony, HyperDaemon, HyperContinuity, HyperGenesis).\
\'95 Layer 5 \'96 Ultra\
Ecosystem-scale cognition and self-evolving OS behavior (Cognitive Twins, Strategy Garden, Reality Twin Mesh, Temporal Backtesting, Law-of-the-OS, Cognitive Economy).\
\'95 Layer 6 \'96 Supreme\
Ontological and civilizational meta-layer (Ontological Compiler, Canon of Truth, Reality Contracts, Human\'96System Co-Evolution, Law of Work & Meaning).\
\'95 Layer 7 \'96 Ascend\
Sovereign norms and obligation stack (Obligation Sentinel, Latent Breach Detector, Norm Collision & Treaty Engine, Constitutional Policy VM, Decision-Proof Ledger, Governance Shells).\
\'95 17.1.3 Cross-Layer Invariants\
Across all layers:\
Governance Supremacy All capabilities are subordinate to:\
Policy & Governance Engine (Section 10), \'a7 Law-of-the-OS & AI Court (17.6.5), \'a7 Constitutional Policy VM (17.8.4) where enabled.\
\uc0\u9675  No layer may bypass:\
Policy evaluation, \'a7 Audit logging (Ledger + Logbook), \'a7 Kill-switch hooks. 1. Ledger-First Evidence Every material action (plans, executions, policy changes, simulations, obligations) produces Ledger events with stable schemas.\
\uc0\u9675  These events must be sufficient for:\
Replay in Temporal Backtesting Engine (17.6.4), \'a7 Forensics (Record Auditor & Logbook), \'a7 Law-of-the-OS adjudication. 2. Capsule-Native Expression Higher-order behaviors (ARC, HyperMesh, Ontological Compiler, etc.) are expressed as:\
Capsules, \'a7 Capsule graphs, \'a7 Or Capsule-like meta-objects.\
\uc0\u9675  They run via the same execution fabric, driver abstractions, and governance as normal automation.\
3. Explainability & Auditability Every layer must provide explanations and evidence at its own level:\
ARC \uc0\u8594  research program plans and alternatives, \'a7 HyperDaemon \u8594  systemic risk graphs and rationale, \'a7 Law-of-the-OS \u8594  case dossiers, precedents, and policy evaluations, \'a7 Ascend \u8594  obligation and norm state explanations. 4. Monotone Dependencies Layer N can depend on layers \u8804  N, but must not assume layers > N exist.\
\uc0\u9675  Lower layers must degrade gracefully if higher layers are disabled or partially present.\
5. Advisory vs Actuation Modes All higher-layer capabilities must support:\
Advisory Mode \'96 observe, analyze, and propose plans/changes. \'a7 Actuation Mode \'96 allowed (per tenant) to trigger Capsules and policy changes under stricter controls.\
\uc0\u9675  Default for Layers 3\'967 is Advisory Mode; Actuation is opt-in and policy-gated.\
6. Tenant Primacy & Progressive Disclosure Capabilities are enabled per tenant / deployment via:\
Feature flags, \'a7 Config, \'a7 Licensing and governance approvals.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
7. Tenants can:\
Run only Layer 1, \'a7 Layer 1 + 2, \'a7 Or specific subsets of higher layers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

