\'95 18.5 System Execution Feature & Use-Case Atlas\
(Unix / Kernel Interface + Package & Environment Drivers) This section is a focused atlas for P2 (Unix / Kernel Execution) and P3 (Package & Environment):\
It shows how System Execution manifests as visible features, buttons, flows, and Capsules.\
\'95 It anchors Sections 5 (Drivers), 8 (Capsules), 10 (Policy), 11 (Observability), 12\'9613 (Reliability/Deployment) in\
concrete usage.\
\'95 18.5.1 Purpose, Responsibilities & Scope\
Purpose Provide a cross-workspace view of:\
Direct Unix command execution (local & remote).\
\uc0\u9675  Env provisioning and convergence.\
\uc0\u9675  Binding commands/env actions into Tasks, Capsules, Workflows, and Workspaces.\
\'95 Responsibilities\
Enumerate feature-level primitives on top of:\
OS Drivers (P1),\
\uc0\u9675  Unix / Kernel Execution (P2),\
\uc0\u9675  Package & Env Drivers (P3).\
\'95 Map each primitive to:\
Primary Workspaces,\
\uc0\u9675  Control-plane components,\
\uc0\u9675  Governance/audit hooks.\
\'95 Scope\
Includes System Execution usage across:\
Master Stack & Projects,\
\uc0\u9675  Dev/DevOps/CI-CD,\
\uc0\u9675  Research & Simulation,\
\uc0\u9675  Writer/Creator pipelines,\
\uc0\u9675  Archive & Logbook,\
\uc0\u9675  Cybersecurity,\
\uc0\u9675  Business/Finance,\
\uc0\u9675  Governance / Audit / Billing,\
\uc0\u9675  Capsules & Marketplace,\
\uc0\u9675  Reliability & Self-Healing,\
\uc0\u9675  UX & Developer Experience.\
\'95 18.5.2 Core System Execution Layer Capabilities\
Governed, auditable execution of Unix commands:\
Local per-project, shared tenant contexts, or isolated sandboxes.\
\uc0\u9675  Remote via secure protocols (SSH/agents) with host profiles and env tags.\
\'95 Capture:\
stdout, stderr, exit code, duration, optional resource metrics.\
\'95 Safety primitives:\
Command/argument allowlists/denylists.\
\uc0\u9675  Risk tiers (read-only, write, privileged).\
\uc0\u9675  Time/CPU/memory limits.\
\'a0\
\'a0\
\'95 Constrained working dirs and mount patterns.\
\uc0\u9675  Interfaces\
Control Plane:\
execute_unix_command(...) \uc0\u8594  handle,\
\uc0\u9675  poll_execution_status(...),\
\uc0\u9675  fetch_execution_result(...).\
\'95 Events:\
ExecutionRequested, ExecutionStarted, ExecutionCompleted/Failed/Killed\
\uc0\u9675  Always linked to actor, workspace, project, policy decision, and Ledger entries.\
\'95 18.5.3 Master Stack & Project Integration\
System-Action Tasks Tasks may embed an execution_plan (command, env, success criteria).\
\uc0\u9675  \'93Run Task\'94 triggers CLI execution; task state advances based on results.\
\'95 Project Runbooks\
Structured sequences of CLI steps (build, migrate, restart, verify).\
\uc0\u9675  Can be run manually or via Capsules.\
\'95 Scheduled System Jobs\
Backups, compaction, ETL; triggered via internal scheduler or external cron through execution adapters.\
\'95 Design Implication\
Projects become operationally complete: \'93done\'94 has explicit System Execution semantics.\
\'95 18.5.4 Engineering / DevOps / CI-CD Flows\
Build/Test/Deploy Runners:\
CLI steps for build, lint, test, deploy; logs & artifacts collected.\
\'95 Dev Environment Bootstrap:\
Clone repo, install via package managers, init DBs, run migrations & smoke tests.\
\'95 Regression Triage:\
On failure, re-run targeted tests, capture logs, attach to Dev workspace tasks.\
\'95 Automated Rollback:\
Pre-defined CLI sequences to revert deployments and restore state.\
\'95 Integration with Dev capabilities:\
Merge Advisor:\
Uses System Execution to trial merges and tests before recommendations.\
\'95 Commit\uc0\u8594 Task:\
Generates tasks that bind diffs to CLI actions (migrations, tooling upgrades).\
\'95 18.5.5 Data / ETL / Analytics / Research Execution\
ETL & Data Pipelines:\
Use DB CLIs, curl/wget, custom binaries for extract/transform/load.\
\'95 Scheduler Integration:\
Interact with cron, slurm, pbs, airflow CLIs for job submission and status.\
\'95 Research & Simulation:\
Launch python, Rscript, matlab, compiled binaries; chain CLI steps into Capsules.\
\'95 Each pipeline step is a System Execution node:\
With metrics, logs, and status aggregated into pipeline dashboards.\
\'95 Failures result in partial pipeline status and remediation Capsule suggestions.\
\'95 18.5.6 Writer / Creator & Content Pipelines\
Content Builds:\
pandoc, LaTeX, ebook CLIs; multi-format outputs (PDF/EPUB/HTML).\
\'95 Media Processing:\
ffmpeg, imagemagick pipelines for encoding, compression, thumbnails, audio post.\
