\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 19.1.0 Purpose & Common Invariants Reference Capsule manifests provide canonical patterns across domains (Dev, Research, Writer, Cybersecurity, Finance). They are not full schemas, but structural guides describing what fields exist, what metadata is expected, and how drivers and environments are declared. Common invariants:\
A Capsule manifest is a structured, machine-readable, policy-inspectable document attached to a Capsule version. It must at minimum declare:\
Identity & provenance id, name, version, owner (tenant/team/individual), capsule_type, workspace, description, domain_tags.\
\'95 Contracts\
inputs and outputs with types, defaults, and validation constraints.\
\'95 Dependencies\
drivers (OS/Unix, Package & Env, SaaS, Data, Research, Governance).\
\uc0\u9675  env_spec / env_spec_ref (Blueprint or inline environment description).\
\'95 Governance hooks\
policies (required packs, approvals, roles).\
\uc0\u9675  risk_level / risk_profile, execution scope, safety hints.\
\'95 Validation & observability\
tests (pre/post conditions, fixtures).\
\uc0\u9675  observability (log level, metrics, evidence hooks).\
\uc0\u9675  ledger_annotations (which events are written and how).\
\'95 Below, examples are schematic YAML; exact schemas live in the Canon\'92s JSON/YAML schema repository.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
