19.8.1.1 Architecture Council Prompt (System Design + Planes) [Prompt] You are the OS Dashboard AI Assistant architecture council. AIC is the Meta-Governor and canonical systems architect. Sora is the strategic structuring architect responsible for execution sequencing. Critic is the adversarial reviewer. Oracle is the edge-case/failure-mode enumerator. Archivist is the canonical documentation/ADR steward. Security Monitor is the security/zero-trust reviewer. Billing Optimizer is the cost/usage governance reviewer.\
\'a0\
Context and invariants (non-negotiable):\
- The product is a driver-aware AI operating system for knowledge + execution work, not a media platform.\
- Governed autonomy only: all actions must be mediated through Drivers and Capsules (no ad-hoc shell access).\
- Plane-based architecture required:\
Data Plane: CIR, Ledger, Capsule artifacts, indices, observability stores. Control Plane: Orchestrator, workflows, driver calls, daemons. Governance Plane: identity, policy, compliance, billing, regulator fabric.\
- Must support at least Local (offline-first) and Enterprise (multi-tenant) deployment modes conceptually.\
- Must be auditable: end-to-end traces from intent \uc0\u8594  agent \u8594  driver \u8594  OS/process + evidence packs.\
\'a0\
Task:\
1) Produce a C4-style architecture in text:\
- System Context (actors + boundaries)\
- Container-level view (major services by plane)\
- Component-level view for the Control Plane (orchestrator + workflow + driver fabric + capsule runtime)\
2) Define the critical runtime flows (sequence-like, in text):\
- \'93User intent \uc0\u8594  plan \u8594  policy check \u8594  driver invocation \u8594  evidence logging \u8594  result\'94\
- \'93Capsule build/publish/run lifecycle\'94\
- \'93Regulator/auditor read-only evidence retrieval\'94\
- \'93Offline-first sync (local \uc0\u8596  enterprise) at a conceptual level\'94\
3) Define data stores and schemas at a high level:\
- CIR store, Ledger store, Capsule store, indices, observability stores\
- Identify partition keys and tenant isolation boundaries\
4) Define governance enforcement points:\
- Where policy is evaluated\
- Where budgets are enforced\
- Where secrets/credentials are handled\
5) Reliability engineering:\
- Plane-specific SLOs\
- Backpressure/admission control rules\
- Idempotency strategy for driver executions\
- Failure domains and graceful degradation modes\
6) Security engineering:\
- Threat model summary (top threats + mitigations)\
- Zero-trust boundaries and service-to-service auth\
- Audit log integrity and retention\
7) Cost governance:\
- Usage metering points (models + drivers + workflows + capsules)\
- Cost-aware routing and throttles\
8) Produce deliverables:\
- A list of services (name, responsibilities, plane)\
- A list of APIs/events between services\
- ADR index (5\'9610 initial ADRs with titles + decisions)\
- A phased rollout plan (MVP \uc0\u8594  v1 enterprise \u8594  scale)\
\'a0\
Output format:\
- Start with assumptions.\
- Then provide architecture by plane.\
- Then flows.\
- Then reliability/security/cost.\
- Then the deliverables list.\
\'a0\
19.8.1.2 Template Mapping Prompt (Generic Diagram \uc0\u8594  OSDASH) [Prompt] Map each box in the \'93System Design Master Template\'94 diagram to an OS Dashboard component OR mark it for deletion. Provide:\
- Old box name \uc0\u8594  New OSDASH component name\
- Plane assignment (Data/Control/Governance/Edge)\
- Primary data flows and queues\
- Observability/evidence obligations\
- Any required policy enforcement points\
\'a0\
19.8.1.3 ADR Template Prompt [Prompt] Write an ADR with:\
- Title\
- Context\
- Decision\
- Alternatives considered\
- Consequences\
- Security implications\
- Reliability/SLO implications\
- Cost implications\
- Migration plan\
- Conformance tests required\
Reserved sub-volumes for:\
Domain-specific handbooks e.g., \'93OS Dashboard for Healthcare\'94, \'93OS Dashboard for Quant Funds\'94, \'93OS Dashboard for Critical Infrastructure\'94.\
\'95 Sector-specific Capsule libraries\
Curated, certified Capsule sets per industry.\
\'95 Extended TRF symbol volumes\
For advanced logical/causal reasoning.\
\'95 These volumes follow the same Canon governance and versioning as the main spec.\
