\cf2 19.9.6 Architecture Conformance Suite (Planes, PEPs, Drivers-Only Rule, Trace Completeness)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Goal Continuously verify that implementations conform to the architecture invariants defined in Sections 1\'963 and 10\'9613.\
\'a0\
Minimum Required Checks (examples) Planes separation:\
No direct bypass from Presentation Layer to Driver Execution without Control/Governance mediation.\
\uc0\u9675  Drivers-only execution:\
All system actions occur via Driver Fabric or Capsule Runtime; no ad-hoc shell bypass.\
\uc0\u9675  Policy enforcement points present:\
Edge PEP, Plan PEP, Driver Boundary PEP, Capsule Runtime PEP.\
\uc0\u9675  Trace completeness:\
Given any result, system can reconstruct intent\uc0\u8594 plan\u8594 policy\u8594 execution\u8594 evidence.\
\uc0\u9675  Idempotency compliance:\
Required drivers support idempotency keys; DLQ handling verified.\
\uc0\u9675  Budget enforcement:\
Model calls, driver invocations, and capsule runs reject/require approvals when budgets are exceeded.\
\uc0\u9675  Data residency checks:\
Model routing and evidence storage obey policy constraints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

